# Golden Pocket Reduxe

- url: https://www.tradingview.com/script/UFHWANPB-Golden-Pocket-Reduxe/
- type: indicator
- pine_id: PUB;9f85b6e510774f34a11b8d0c2b723b0d
- version: 14.0

## Description

[b]Golden Pocket Reduxe[/b]

Golden Pocket Reduxe is a single overlay that combines two of the most reliable kinds of price levels — Fibonacci Golden Pocket retracement zones and Supply/Demand order blocks — and shows you where they line up. It is built to give you a clean read of where price is most likely to react, across as many timeframes as you want to see at once, without the chart turning into spaghetti.

The Golden Pocket is the area inside a swing where pullbacks most often pause or reverse. The Reduxe applies this concept across multiple timeframes and trading styles at once, and pairs it with order-block detection so you can see when a Fib pullback is also landing on a level where institutional buyers or sellers stepped in.

[b]Why this exists[/b]

Most Golden Pocket indicators draw one set of zones based on one set of pivot rules. That works great, but you might have issues when you change timeframes, switch from stocks to futures, or want to see a 1-hour zone while you trade a 5-minute chart. This indicator was built to address all of that:

[list]
[*]It runs up to five GP setups at once — two on the chart timeframe and three from any higher timeframes you pick — without redrawing the same zone twice.
[*]It detects supply and demand zones the way professional order-block traders do, with filters for break of structure, volume confirmation, and zone shrinkage on retest.
[*]It highlights confluence — places where multiple signals overlap — so you can immediately see the highest-probability levels.
[*]It handles futures session rollovers, non-standard chart types like Heikin Ashi and Renko, and Regular Trading Hours filtering for equities, all without you having to think about it.
[/list]

[b]Golden Pocket zones[/b]

The indicator tracks pivot highs and lows on whatever timeframe you point it at and draws the Golden Pocket retracement band between each pair. Each zone stays anchored to the specific pivot pair that created it, so an unrelated swing on the opposite side of the market does not destroy a still-valid zone. Bullish GPs mark pullback support in uptrends. Bearish GPs mark rally resistance in downtrends. Both can be color-coded, labeled, or hidden independently.

When a new pivot forms in the same direction, the previous zone can either be archived as a Closed GP (kept on the chart in a different color so you can see historical levels that may still matter) or removed entirely. Closed GPs can be cleaned up automatically by max count, by price invalidation, or both.

There is also an optional Active GP invalidation rule: if price closes beyond a zone for a set number of consecutive bars, the zone is closed automatically. While the counter is running, the box border can recolor as a warning so you can see at a glance which zones are about to be invalidated.

[b]Supply and Demand zones[/b]

When an impulsive candle breaks recent structure, the indicator draws an order block at the last opposing candle before the impulse — the precise level where the previous side lost control. This is the classic order-block construction, not a wide consolidation range.

The S/D engine includes:

[list]
[*][b]Break of Structure filter[/b] — only confirm a zone when the impulse actually breaks the recent high or low, not just any large candle inside a range. Toggleable.
[*][b]Shrink on retest[/b] — each time price comes back to a zone, it shrinks from the tested edge to visually represent orders being absorbed. After the configured number of retests, the zone is removed.
[*][b]Cross-invalidation[/b] — opposing zones that overlap heavily are automatically removed, since they cannot both be valid.
[*][b]Volume protection[/b] — high-volume zones (marked with a ★) resist invalidation from weaker opposing impulses.
[*][b]Overlap deduplication[/b] — prevents the same level from being marked twice.
[/list]

[b]Persistent GPs (Day / Week / Month)[/b]

Three calendar-period boxes drawn from the live High and Low of the current calendar day, week, or month. These are different from pivot-based GPs — they update continuously as the period's range expands and reset cleanly at the start of each new period. Each period has its own enable toggle, color, fib levels, position, label, midpoint extension, and Regular Trading Hours mode. They are anchored to calendar boundaries in the symbol's timezone, which means they stay stable across futures session rollovers and behave the same way on every symbol.

Useful for higher-timeframe context that does not move as fast as pivot-based GPs, intraday targets off the day range, and weekly or monthly bias zones for swing trading.

[b]Profiles[/b]

Instead of forcing you to manually retune pivot distance, ATR multiplier, and zone height every time you change charts, the indicator ships with preset bundles tuned for different trading styles:

[list]
[*][b]Auto[/b] — picks the best profile based on the chart's timeframe.
[*][b]Scalping[/b] — tighter pivots and faster zones, suited to charts under 5 minutes.
[*][b]Intraday[/b] — balanced settings for session trading on 15–30 minute charts.
[*][b]Swing[/b] — wider, slower zones for institutional levels on 1-hour charts and above.
[*][b]Custom[/b] — full manual control over every parameter.
[/list]

GP profiles and S/D profiles are independent — you can run a Scalping GP and a Swing S/D on the same chart, or any other combination.

[b]Multi-timeframe layout[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Chart GP Profile 1 / 2[/b] — two profile slots that draw on the chart timeframe with no higher-timeframe lag. Each has its own color.
[*][b]Overlay Timeframe 1 / 2 / 3[/b] — three slots that each have their own timeframe, GP profile checkboxes (Scalping, Intraday, Swing, Custom), and S/D profile selector. If an overlay slot's timeframe matches the chart and a chart profile already covers that profile, the overlay slot suppresses just that profile to avoid drawing the same zone twice.
[/list]

So a typical setup might be: chart Profile 1 set to Auto for the chart timeframe, Overlay TF1 set to 1H for medium-term context, and Overlay TF2 set to 4H for higher-timeframe bias — all running simultaneously, each with its own color, all drawn on the same chart.

[b]Confluence detection[/b]

Automatically highlights places where two GPs overlap, or where a GP overlaps an S/D zone. Confluence boxes are drawn in their own color and labeled "GP + GP" or "GP + S/D" so you can immediately tell which kind of agreement you're looking at. These are typically the highest-probability levels on the chart.

[b]Volume enhancement[/b]

Zones that form on above-average volume are visually boosted (more opaque) and marked with a ★ in the label. The intuition is simple: a level made by real participation is more likely to hold than one made by thin price action. The volume MA length and the opacity boost are both configurable.

[b]MA filter[/b]

Optional trend filter that restricts which GP boxes are drawn based on a configurable Fast/Slow MA pair. You can filter by trend direction (only draw GPs that align with the trend), by price position (only draw GPs whose pivots are on the right side of the MA), or turn the filter off entirely. Each MA has its own type (SMA or EMA), length, color, and line style (Solid / Dashed / Dotted).

[b]Use Real OHLC[/b]

Forces the indicator to use actual market prices on non-standard chart types like Heikin Ashi, Renko, and Kagi. Without this, pivots and zones would be drawn from modified candle values that don't reflect real traded levels, and your entries, exits, and alerts would all sit at the wrong prices. Keep this on unless you specifically want zones based on the chart's modified candles.

[b]Alerts[/b]

Two alert paths, usable independently or together:

[list]
[*][b]Specific conditions[/b] — pick from the dropdown: Bull GP Touch, Bear GP Touch, Day GP Touch, Week GP Touch, Month GP Touch, Demand Zone Touch, Supply Zone Touch, Confluence Zone Touch, or Any Zone Touch.
[*][b]All-Events Alert Stream[/b] — set the alert condition to "Any alert() function call" and every zone touch fires a detailed message with direction, timeframe, profile, and symbol — for example "Bull 15 Intraday Golden Pocket Hit on BTCUSD". Persistent GP touches fire as "Day GP Hit", "Week GP Hit", or "Month GP Hit".
[/list]

[b]Visual customization[/b]

Bull, Bear, Day, Week, Month, and Confluence labels each toggle independently. Volume ★ markers have their own toggle. GP box borders can be Solid, Dashed, or Dotted. Active GPs have separate cosmetic offset inputs that control visual width and position without affecting any underlying calculations. An optional GP anchor dot marks the pivot bar where each zone originated. Midpoint lines can optionally be extended back to the originating pivot to make the zone's history easier to read.

[b]How to start[/b]

[list]
[*]Open Settings → Inputs.
[*]Pick a Chart GP Profile (Auto is a fine default) and a color.
[*]Optionally enable one or more Overlay Timeframe slots if you want higher-timeframe GPs on the same chart.
[*]Leave the S/D engine on its defaults to start; tune later if you want fewer or wider zones.
[*]Enable Persistent GPs (Day / Week / Month) for fixed bias zones that don't depend on pivots.
[*]To set up alerts, right-click the chart → Add alert → set the Condition to this indicator → pick a specific event or choose "Any alert() function call" with the All-Events stream toggle on.
[/list]

[b]Credit[/b]

Based on the original Golden Pocket script by [url=https://www.tradingview.com/u/TradingWolf/]TradingWolf[/url], heavily extended from there.

Most features were inspired by Terry ([url=https://www.tradingview.com/u/Terryztrade/]Terryztrade[/url]), who taught myself and many others the true value of fibs.

Alert plumbing uses the RecursiveAlerts library by [url=https://www.tradingview.com/u/HeWhoMustNotBeNamed/]HeWhoMustNotBeNamed[/url].

[b]License[/b]

Open-source under the Mozilla Public License 2.0.

## Source Code

````pine
// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// © TradingWolf (heavily modified by Cramp/MissingMarsupial)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// GP Reduxe — Multi-Timeframe Golden Pocket + Supply/Demand indicator
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Plots Golden Pocket (0.618–0.707 Fib) zones from pivot highs/lows, plus
// supply/demand zones from impulse candles, and highlights where they overlap.
//
// ─── Architecture ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// • Chart GP Profile 1/2 — two profile slots that draw GP zones on the
//   chart timeframe (no request.security, so no HTF lag). Each has its own
//   box color; if both resolve to the same profile, Profile 1 wins and the
//   zone is drawn once.
// • Overlay Timeframe 1/2/3 — each slot has its own TF + up to 4 GP profiles
//   (Scalping/Intraday/Swing/Custom) and its own S/D profile resolution
//   (with an Off option to suppress S/D for that slot).
//   Per-profile dedup: if a slot's TF matches the chart and a chart profile
//   already covers that profile, the overlay slot suppresses only that
//   profile (other ticked profiles on the same slot still draw).
// • S/D zones — always computed on chart data; the active S/D profile is
//   chosen by whichever overlay slot's TF matches the chart TF (or Auto).
//   If that slot's S/D profile is Off, no S/D zones are drawn.
// • Persistent GPs (Day / Week / Month) — boxes drawn from the prior
//   COMPLETED period's High/Low, pulled from the daily/weekly/monthly series
//   (same source as the Prior Period Levels lines, high[1]/low[1] +
//   lookahead_on, so they're non-repainting and read identically on every
//   chart timeframe). Each has its own fib levels, color, position, label
//   toggle, and optional RTH-only mode for equities/futures.
// • FVG zones (optional) — ICT Fair Value Gaps detected on the chart
//   timeframe: three-candle imbalances that price often revisits. They feed
//   confluence, alerts, and the dashboard like any other zone.
// • Confluence — highlights GP+GP or GP+S/D overlaps in a single color;
//   optional label text distinguishes which type.
// • Active GP invalidation — optional: closes a GP after N consecutive bars
//   close beyond the zone. Warn-before-invalidation recolors the border
//   during the counter so at-risk zones are visible before they're killed.
//
// ─── GP redraw rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Bull and bear GPs are anchored to the specific pivot pair that defined
// them. A new pivot HIGH archives/redraws the bull GP only; a new pivot LOW
// archives/redraws the bear GP only. Opposite-side pivots leave the existing
// zone alone, so a GP isn't destroyed by an unrelated swing on the other
// side of the range.
//
// ─── Profile defaults (pivot distance) ────────────────────────────────────
// Scalping 2 · Intraday 5 · Swing 10 · Custom user-set.
//
// ─── Performance notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// • Each overlay slot makes ONE combined data request (all four pivot
//   profiles + Quick range in a single tuple); fully disabled slots skip it.
// • A per-bar Zone Registry collects every active box once; alerts,
//   confluence, and alert conditions all loop over it instead of
//   enumerating each slot/profile by hand.
// • Pivot-pair derived math inside drawGP (range, fib edges, MA filter,
//   volume flags) only runs on bars where a pivot just formed.
// • Confluence rebuilds only when a GP or S/D zone actually changes.
// • Chart-TF MA pair is skipped when the filter is off and neither plot is
//   shown; per-TF MA security calls are skipped when the filter is off.
// • Volume MA is skipped when volume enhancement is off.
// • Real-OHLC security call is skipped when Use Real OHLC is off.
// • Active GP boxes have cosmetic left/right offsets (pure visuals — no
//   effect on pivot, invalidation, or volume calculations).
//
// ─── Visual toggles ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Bull GP, Bear GP, Day GP, Week GP, Month GP, and Confluence labels each
// toggle independently. ★ volume markers (on GP and S/D labels) have their
// own toggle.
//
// ─── Status line ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// All inputs are flagged display = display.none so the chart's status line
// and Data Window stay clean (no flood of input values). Settings menu and
// indicator behavior are unaffected — this is purely a readout filter. To
// expose any specific input in the status line, change its display flag to
// display.status_line (or display.all).
//
// ─── Alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two ways to set up alerts in TradingView's Add-alert dialog:
//   1. Pick a specific Condition from the dropdown — Bull GP Touch, Bear GP
//      Touch, Bull GP Extension Touch, Bear GP Extension Touch, Day GP Touch,
//      Week GP Touch, Month GP Touch, Demand Zone Touch, Supply Zone Touch,
//      FVG Touch, Confluence Zone Touch, Any Zone Touch, or Approaching Any
//      Zone (early warning when price gets within N ATR of a zone edge). Use
//      this when
//      you only want one event type.
//   2. Set Condition to "Any alert() function call" with the All-Events
//      Alert Stream input on. Every zone touch fires a detailed message
//      embedding direction/timeframe/profile (e.g. "Bull 15 Intraday Golden
//      Pocket Hit on BTCUSD", "Bull 15 Intraday GP Extension Hit on BTCUSD").
//      Persistent GP touches fire as "Day GP Hit", "Week GP Hit", or "Month
//      GP Hit"; persistent extension touches fire as "Day GP Extension Hit",
//      etc. Use this when you want one alert covering everything.
//
// License: Mozilla Public License 2.0
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

//@version=6
import HeWhoMustNotBeNamed/RecursiveAlerts/2 as al
// calc_bars_count caps the historical bars the script processes on initial
// load. Real-time calculations are unaffected. Pine requires a const int
// here, so this isn't user-overridable from the Inputs tab — but TradingView
// auto-exposes a "Calculated bars" override under Settings → Calculation
// (set 0 there for unlimited).
//
// 5000 is chosen because the overlay-TF slots need enough CHART history to
// cover their own timeframe's pivot warmup — a Daily Swing pivot needs ~40
// daily bars, which is far more than 500 one-minute bars (~8 hours). At 500,
// TF2/TF3 daily GPs silently never formed on low-timeframe charts. 5000
// covers a Daily overlay down to ~5m charts (regular-hours symbols); for a
// Daily overlay on a 1m chart, set "Calculated bars" to 0 (unlimited) under
// Settings → Calculation.
indicator(title = 'Golden Pocket Reduxe', shorttitle = 'GP Reduxe', overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, calc_bars_count = 5000)

//#region Inputs
chartGpGroup = '=== Chart GPs ==='
fib_preset = input.string('Custom', title = 'Fib Preset', options = ['Custom', 'Wide (0.65 / 0.707)', 'Classic GP (0.618 / 0.65)', 'ICT OTE (0.62 / 0.79)'], group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Ready-made retracement bands for the pivot and Quick GPs (chart + overlay timeframes).\n\nCustom — uses the Fib Level 1 / 2 inputs below (default 0.65 / 0.707, unchanged from before).\nWide — the 0.65–0.707 band, same as the Custom defaults.\nClassic GP — the traditional tighter Golden Pocket, 0.618–0.65.\nICT OTE — the Optimal Trade Entry window, 0.62–0.79, the full discount/premium zone used in ICT-style trading. Pairs well with the OTE Sweet Spot Line below marking 0.705 inside it.\n\nAlso reshapes the GP Extension bands, which mirror the same spacing beyond the swing. Persistent Day/Week/Month GPs keep their own fib inputs and are not affected.', display = display.none)
fib_level_1 = input.float(0.65, title = 'Fib Level 1', group = chartGpGroup, inline = '0', tooltip = 'Only used when Fib Preset is Custom. Upper and lower edges of the Golden Pocket retracement band. Defaults 0.65 / 0.707 define a wider zone spanning the 65% and 70.7% Fibonacci retracements. Use 0.618 / 0.65 for the classic, tighter GP. The GP box spans from Fib Level 1 to Fib Level 2.\n\nThese values also drive the GP Extension target bands when those are enabled — the extension box mirrors this same fib spacing on the opposite side of the pivot pair.', display = display.none)
fib_level_2 = input.float(0.707, title = 'Fib Level 2', group = chartGpGroup, inline = '0', display = display.none)
show_ote_line = input.bool(false, title = 'OTE Sweet Spot Line', group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'ote', tooltip = 'Draw a dotted line inside each active GP at the 0.705 retracement — the sweet spot of the ICT Optimal Trade Entry window, often used as the precise entry trigger inside the zone. Drawn in the GP\'s own color for pivot and Quick GPs on the chart and overlay timeframes.\n\nMost useful with the ICT OTE preset (the line sits inside the 0.62–0.79 window), but it works with any band that contains the level.', display = display.none)
ote_line_level = input.float(0.705, title = 'Level', minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.005, group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'ote', tooltip = 'Retracement level for the sweet-spot line. 0.705 is the ICT standard; 0.618 or 0.786 are common alternatives.', display = display.none)

// Resolve the effective fib band from the preset (Custom = the inputs above).
_fibL1 = fib_preset == 'Classic GP (0.618 / 0.65)' ? 0.618 : fib_preset == 'ICT OTE (0.62 / 0.79)' ? 0.62 : fib_preset == 'Wide (0.65 / 0.707)' ? 0.65 : fib_level_1
_fibL2 = fib_preset == 'Classic GP (0.618 / 0.65)' ? 0.65 : fib_preset == 'ICT OTE (0.62 / 0.79)' ? 0.79 : fib_preset == 'Wide (0.65 / 0.707)' ? 0.707 : fib_level_2
show_gp_ext = input.bool(false, title = 'GP Extensions', group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'gp_ext', tooltip = 'Project an extension target band beyond each swing high/low pair. The bullish extension sits above the pivot high (upside target after the bull GP holds); the bearish extension sits below the pivot low (downside target after the bear GP holds).\n\nThe extension band uses the same Fib Level 1 / Fib Level 2 values as the GP retracement, mirrored to the opposite side of the swing. With default 0.65 / 0.707 inputs the extension band lands between the classic 1.65 and 1.707 Fibonacci extension levels — just past the popular 1.618 target. To target the classic 1.618 exactly, set Fib Level 1 to 0.618 (this also tightens the GP retracement to the classic Golden Pocket band).\n\nExtensions draw whenever a valid swing exists, independent of the MA filter or invalidation rules — useful for seeing potential targets even when no active GP is currently drawn.', display = display.none)
show_gp_ext_line = input.bool(false, title = 'Bonus Line', group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'gp_ext', tooltip = 'Optional standalone extension line drawn at a user-defined Fibonacci extension level (defaults to 1.272). Independent of the Extension band — enable either, both, or neither.\n\nThe line is drawn in each GP\'s color: bull line above the pivot high, bear line below the pivot low. Useful for traders who want a single classic extension target (1.272, 1.618, 2.0, 2.618) without the full band.', display = display.none)
gp_ext_line_level = input.float(1.272, title = 'Level', group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'gp_ext', tooltip = 'Fibonacci extension level for the Bonus Line. Standard targets: 1.272, 1.414, 1.618, 2.0, 2.618. Values at or below 1.0 would fall inside the swing — use the GP retracement band for that range.', display = display.none)
ext_link_invalidation = input.bool(true, title = 'Clear Extension on GP Invalidation', group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'When an active GP is invalidated, also remove its extension target. The extension projects the move that follows the GP holding, so once the GP fails the target no longer applies. Only affects swing GP extensions, and only when Invalidate Active GP is on.', display = display.none)
ext_mark_reached = input.bool(true, title = 'Mark Reached Extensions', group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'ext_reached', tooltip = 'Recolor a GP extension once price reaches it, so you can see at a glance which targets have been tagged. The band stays on the chart in the reached color — handy for watching how price behaves at the level (rejection, retest, continuation).', display = display.none)
ext_reached_color = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 55), title = '', group = chartGpGroup, inline = 'ext_reached', display = display.none)
chart_gp_profile_1 = input.string('Auto', title = 'Chart GP Profile 1', options = ['Off', 'Auto', 'Scalping', 'Intraday', 'Swing', 'Quick'], group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Primary GP profile drawn on the chart timeframe. Most users only need this one.\n\nOff — No chart-TF GPs from this slot.\n\nAuto — Picks based on chart timeframe:\n• ≤5 min → Scalping\n• 6–30 min → Intraday\n• >30 min (1H+) → Swing\nSwitching charts will switch which profile is drawn. Use a fixed profile below if you want consistent coverage across all charts.\n\nScalping / Intraday / Swing — Fixed selection regardless of chart timeframe.\n\nQuick — Draws a GP immediately from the highest and lowest price over a set number of recent bars, without waiting for a swing to confirm — like glancing at the recent range and marking the pocket by eye. The bar count auto-sizes to the chart timeframe; change it with Quick Profile Lookback below.\n\nPivot presets:\nScalping: 1–5m → 2 · 6–30m → 4 · 1H–4H → 6 · Daily+ → 8\nIntraday: 1–5m → 3 · 6–30m → 6 · 1H–4H → 10 · Daily+ → 15\nSwing:    1–5m → 5 · 6–30m → 8 · 1H–4H → 15 · Daily+ → 20', display = display.none)
chart_gp_profile_2 = input.string('Off', title = 'Chart GP Profile 2', options = ['Off', 'Scalping', 'Intraday', 'Swing', 'Quick'], group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Optional second chart-timeframe profile to stack on top of Profile 1. Example: Profile 1 = Scalping + Profile 2 = Swing draws both Scalping and Swing GPs on the current chart. If both profiles resolve to the same value, the zone is drawn once.\n\nOverlap with TF1/TF2/TF3: if an overlay slot\'s timeframe matches the chart and it has a profile ticked that a chart profile already draws, the overlay slot\'s checkbox for that profile is suppressed to avoid drawing the same zone twice. Chart profiles win.', display = display.none)
quick_lookback_in = input.int(0, title = 'Quick Profile Lookback', minval = 0, group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'How many recent bars the Quick profile looks back over to find its high and low.\n\n0 = automatic, based on the timeframe the Quick GP is drawn on:\n• 5 min and under → 50 bars\n• 6–30 min → 40 bars\n• 1H–4H → 30 bars\n• Daily and up → 20 bars\n\nSet any number above 0 to use that exact bar count everywhere Quick is turned on.', display = display.none)
chart_gp_box_color = input.color(color.new(#FFD700, 80), title = 'Chart GP Box Color 1', group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Box color for GPs drawn by profile 1. Per-timeframe overlay slots (TF1/TF2/TF3) use their own colors.', display = display.none)
chart_gp_box_color_2 = input.color(color.new(#40E0D0, 80), title = 'Chart GP Box Color 2', group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Box color for GPs drawn by profile 2. Per-timeframe overlay slots (TF1/TF2/TF3) use their own colors.', display = display.none)
use_real_ohlc = input.bool(true, title = 'Use Real OHLC', group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Uses real market prices instead of the modified values your chart style displays.\n\nHeikin Ashi recalculates every candle\'s open and close, and after gaps it can shift highs and lows as well — so with this OFF, zones can sit at prices that never actually traded. With this ON, all zones are built from real traded prices and are safe to use on Heikin Ashi charts.\n\nKeep this ON unless you specifically want zones based on your chart\'s candle style.', display = display.none)
show_ha_warning = input.bool(true, title = 'Heikin Ashi Warning', group = chartGpGroup, tooltip = 'Show a label on the chart when Heikin Ashi is detected while Use Real OHLC is OFF — zones are then built from smoothed Heikin Ashi prices, which can add extra S/D signals and shift levels away from prices that actually traded. With Use Real OHLC on, zones already use real prices, so no warning is shown.', display = display.none)

activeGpGroup = '=== Active GP Behavior ==='
gp_invalidation_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Invalidate Active GP', group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_inv', tooltip = 'Close active GPs when price invalidates them for N consecutive bars. Bull GP invalidates below the box bottom. Bear GP invalidates above the box top.', display = display.none)
gp_invalidation_source = input.string('Open', title = 'Source', options = ['Close', 'Open'], group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_inv', display = display.none)
gp_invalidation_bars = input.int(3, title = 'Bars', minval = 1, group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_inv', tooltip = 'Consecutive bars required to invalidate an active GP box.', display = display.none)
gp_warn_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Warn Before Invalidation', group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_warn', tooltip = 'Visually flag active GPs whose invalidation counter has started but not yet reached the threshold. Recolors the box border so you see at a glance which zones are one or two bars from being invalidated. Only meaningful when Invalidate Active GP is on.', display = display.none)
gp_warn_color = input.color(color.new(color.red, 20), title = '', group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_warn', display = display.none)
gp_oop_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Out of Play Highlight', group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_oop', tooltip = 'Highlight active GPs that are not yet in a position for price to react to them. A Bull GP (support zone) is out of play when price is below it — price would need to come back up before it matters. A Bear GP (resistance zone) is out of play when price is above it.\n\nBlue border = zone exists but is not in play. No extra border = zone is in position. Orange border = zone is about to be invalidated (if that feature is on).', display = display.none)
gp_oop_color = input.color(color.new(#4488FF, 20), title = '', group = activeGpGroup, inline = 'gp_oop', display = display.none)
gp_left_offset = input.int(3, title = 'Active GP Left Offset (bars)', minval = 0, group = activeGpGroup, tooltip = 'How many bars back from the current bar the left edge of each active GP box is drawn. Purely cosmetic — does not affect pivot, invalidation, or volume calculations. The box is anchored to the current bar and slides forward with it.\n\nCombine with Right Offset to control the active box\'s visual width and position.', display = display.none)
gp_right_offset = input.int(10, title = 'Active GP Right Offset (bars)', minval = 0, group = activeGpGroup, tooltip = 'How many bars past the current bar the right edge is drawn. See Left Offset for details.', display = display.none)

closedGpGroup = '=== Closed GPs ==='
show_closed = input.bool(true, title = 'Show Closed GPs', group = closedGpGroup, inline = 'closed', tooltip = 'Keep old GP boxes on the chart when new pivots form. Closed boxes are recolored and stop extending — useful for seeing historical support/resistance levels that may still be relevant.', display = display.none)
closed_color = input.color(color.new(color.gray, 85), title = '', group = closedGpGroup, inline = 'closed', display = display.none)
closed_deletion = input.string('Both', title = 'Removal', options = ['Max Count', 'Price Invalidation', 'Both'], group = closedGpGroup, tooltip = 'How closed GP boxes are removed from the chart.\n\nMax Count — Keeps a fixed number of closed boxes per timeframe slot. Oldest are removed first.\n\nPrice Invalidation — Removes a closed box when price closes beyond it (below a Bull GP or above a Bear GP), indicating the level has been decisively broken.\n\nBoth — Applies both rules. Whichever triggers first removes the box.', display = display.none)
max_closed = input.int(4, title = 'Max Closed GPs', minval = 1, group = closedGpGroup, tooltip = 'Maximum closed GP boxes kept per timeframe slot. Oldest are removed first. Only applies when Removal includes Max Count.\n\nExample: 4 per slot × 3 TF slots = up to 12 closed boxes on chart.', display = display.none)

persistGpGroup = '=== Persistent GPs ==='
show_day_gp = input.bool(true, title = 'Enable Day GP', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'day_gp', tooltip = 'Persistent GPs are anchored to a fixed time period (Day / Week / Month) instead of swing pivots. Each box is drawn from the PRIOR completed period\'s High and Low — the same levels as the Prior Period Levels lines — so it stays fixed all period, never repaints, and reads identically on every chart timeframe. It updates once at each new period\'s start, when the finished period hands over its range.\n\nUseful for: higher-timeframe context that doesn\'t change as fast as pivot-based GPs, intraday targets off the prior day\'s range, weekly/monthly bias zones for swing trading.\n\nEach period has independent fib levels, color, position, and label so you can stack all three without visual conflict.', display = display.none)
day_gp_color = input.color(color.new(color.teal, 80), title = '', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'day_gp', display = display.none)
day_gp_fib_1 = input.float(0.65, title = 'Day GP Fib Level 1', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'day_gp_fib', tooltip = 'Upper and lower edges of the Day GP retracement band. Independent from chart GP fib levels and from Week/Month fibs so you can use different bands per period (e.g. classic tighter 0.618/0.65 on Day while Week/Month use the wider 0.65/0.707).', display = display.none)
day_gp_fib_2 = input.float(0.707, title = 'Day GP Fib Level 2', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'day_gp_fib', display = display.none)
day_gp_rth_only = input.bool(false, title = 'Day GP RTH Only', group = persistGpGroup, tooltip = 'When enabled, the period uses only Regular Trading Hours (based on the symbol\'s session) to determine the High/Low used for the GP. Useful for equities/futures where overnight price action distorts the range. No effect on 24h symbols (crypto, FX).\n\nWeek/Month each have their own RTH toggle below.', display = display.none)
day_gp_right_offset = input.int(20, title = 'Day Right Offset', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'day_gp_pos', tooltip = 'Bars between the current bar and the right edge of the Day GP box. Positive values push the box into future space (to the right of the current bar, closer to the Y-axis labels). Negative values pull it back behind the current bar.\n\nBy default, Day/Week/Month are staggered so all three are visible at once. Adjust if they overlap with right-edge overlays like VRVP.', display = display.none)
day_gp_width = input.int(18, title = 'Width', minval = 1, group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'day_gp_pos', tooltip = 'Width of the Day GP box in bars.', display = display.none)
day_gp_mid_extend_left = input.bool(false, title = 'Day Midpoint Extend Left', group = persistGpGroup, tooltip = 'When enabled, the Day GP midpoint line extends across the chart to the left.', display = display.none)
show_day_gp_ext = input.bool(false, title = 'Day GP Extensions', group = persistGpGroup, tooltip = 'Project an extension target band beyond the Day GP\'s High and Low. Bullish band sits above the day high, bearish band below the day low. Uses the Day GP\'s own Fib Level 1 / Fib Level 2 values (mirrored outward), so default 0.65/0.707 lands at the 1.65/1.707 extensions — just past the popular 1.618 target. Set Fib Level 1 to 0.618 for the classic 1.618. Use the global Persistent GP Bonus Line below for a single classic level (default 1.272).', display = display.none)

show_week_gp = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable Week GP', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'week_gp', tooltip = 'Draw a GP box from the prior completed week\'s High and Low. Updates at the start of each new week. Off by default — enable for swing-trading bias zones.', display = display.none)
week_gp_color = input.color(color.new(color.purple, 80), title = '', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'week_gp', display = display.none)
week_gp_fib_1 = input.float(0.65, title = 'Week GP Fib Level 1', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'week_gp_fib', display = display.none)
week_gp_fib_2 = input.float(0.707, title = 'Week GP Fib Level 2', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'week_gp_fib', display = display.none)
week_gp_right_offset = input.int(44, title = 'Week Right Offset', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'week_gp_pos', display = display.none)
week_gp_width = input.int(18, title = 'Width', minval = 1, group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'week_gp_pos', display = display.none)
week_gp_rth_only = input.bool(false, title = 'Week GP RTH Only', group = persistGpGroup, display = display.none)
week_gp_mid_extend_left = input.bool(false, title = 'Week Midpoint Extend Left', group = persistGpGroup, display = display.none)
show_week_gp_ext = input.bool(false, title = 'Week GP Extensions', group = persistGpGroup, tooltip = 'Same as Day GP Extensions but anchored to the calendar-week High/Low. See Day GP Extensions tooltip for details.', display = display.none)

show_month_gp = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable Month GP', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'month_gp', tooltip = 'Draw a GP box from the prior completed month\'s High and Low. Updates at the start of each new month. Off by default — enable for higher-timeframe bias zones.', display = display.none)
month_gp_color = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 80), title = '', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'month_gp', display = display.none)
month_gp_fib_1 = input.float(0.65, title = 'Month GP Fib Level 1', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'month_gp_fib', display = display.none)
month_gp_fib_2 = input.float(0.707, title = 'Month GP Fib Level 2', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'month_gp_fib', display = display.none)
month_gp_right_offset = input.int(68, title = 'Month Right Offset', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'month_gp_pos', display = display.none)
month_gp_width = input.int(18, title = 'Width', minval = 1, group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'month_gp_pos', display = display.none)
month_gp_rth_only = input.bool(false, title = 'Month GP RTH Only', group = persistGpGroup, display = display.none)
month_gp_mid_extend_left = input.bool(false, title = 'Month Midpoint Extend Left', group = persistGpGroup, display = display.none)
show_month_gp_ext = input.bool(false, title = 'Month GP Extensions', group = persistGpGroup, tooltip = 'Same as Day GP Extensions but anchored to the calendar-month High/Low. See Day GP Extensions tooltip for details.', display = display.none)
show_persistent_ext_line = input.bool(false, title = 'Persistent GP Bonus Line', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'pers_ext_line', tooltip = 'Optional standalone extension line for whichever Day/Week/Month GPs are visible. Drawn at the user-defined Fibonacci extension level set to the right (defaults to 1.272). Independent of each period’s Extension band toggle — enable either, both, or neither.\n\nThe line is drawn in each period’s GP color: bull line above the period high, bear line below the period low.', display = display.none)
persistent_ext_line_level = input.float(1.272, title = 'Level', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'pers_ext_line', tooltip = 'Fibonacci extension level for the Persistent GP Bonus Line. Standard targets: 1.272, 1.414, 1.618, 2.0, 2.618.', display = display.none)
persistent_mid_match_color = input.bool(true, title = 'Persistent Midpoint Matches GP Color', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'pers_mid_col', tooltip = 'When enabled, each persistent GP\'s midpoint line takes its color from that GP\'s box color — Day mid in Day color, Week mid in Week color, Month mid in Month color. Helpful when multiple persistent midpoints extend left across the chart, so you can tell at a glance which line belongs to which period. When disabled, all three midpoints use the custom color picked to the right.', display = display.none)
persistent_mid_color = input.color(color.new(color.white, 30), title = '', group = persistGpGroup, inline = 'pers_mid_col', display = display.none)

priorLevelsGroup = '=== Prior Period Levels ==='
show_pdhl = input.bool(false, title = 'Prior Day H/L', group = priorLevelsGroup, inline = 'pdhl', tooltip = 'Draw horizontal lines at the prior session\'s high and low (PDH / PDL) — the last completed day\'s full range. These are key "draw on liquidity" levels. Fixed for the entire session and update at the start of each new day.', display = display.none)
pdhl_color = input.color(color.new(color.teal, 50), title = '', group = priorLevelsGroup, inline = 'pdhl', display = display.none)
show_pwhl = input.bool(false, title = 'Prior Week H/L', group = priorLevelsGroup, inline = 'pwhl', tooltip = 'Draw horizontal lines at the prior week\'s high and low (PWH / PWL). Updates every Monday.', display = display.none)
pwhl_color = input.color(color.new(color.purple, 50), title = '', group = priorLevelsGroup, inline = 'pwhl', display = display.none)
show_pmhl = input.bool(false, title = 'Prior Month H/L', group = priorLevelsGroup, inline = 'pmhl', tooltip = 'Draw horizontal lines at the prior month\'s high and low (PMH / PML). Updates on the 1st of each month.', display = display.none)
pmhl_color = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 50), title = '', group = priorLevelsGroup, inline = 'pmhl', display = display.none)
show_prior_labels = input.bool(true, title = 'Labels', group = priorLevelsGroup, tooltip = 'Show PDH / PDL / PWH / PWL / PMH / PML text labels that float to the right of the current bar.', display = display.none)
prior_label_offset = input.int(10, title = 'Label Offset (bars)', minval = 0, group = priorLevelsGroup, tooltip = 'How many bars to the right of the current bar the prior-period labels float. Defaults just past the Fib Ladder labels so the two don\'t collide when the ladder is set to Extend Right. The level lines themselves stop at the current bar and do not project right.', display = display.none)
prior_rth_only = input.bool(false, title = 'RTH Only', group = priorLevelsGroup, tooltip = 'Use only Regular Trading Hours to determine prior period highs and lows. Useful for equities and futures where overnight price action distorts the range. No effect on 24h symbols.', display = display.none)
prior_line_style = input.string('Dashed', title = 'Style', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = priorLevelsGroup, display = display.none)

visualGroup = '=== Visuals ==='
show_line = input.bool(false, title = 'Fib Line', inline = '0', group = visualGroup, display = display.none)
line_colour = input.color(color.black, title = '', inline = '0', group = visualGroup, display = display.none)
line_style = input.string(defval = 'Dashed', title = '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], inline = '0', group = visualGroup, display = display.none)
show_bull_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Bull GP', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle', tooltip = 'Toggle each label type independently. Bull/Bear labels appear on active GP boxes; Day/Week/Month GP labels on the persistent calendar-period boxes; Confluence label on overlap boxes; ★ marks zones formed on above-average volume (only meaningful when Volume Enhancement is enabled).', display = display.none)
show_bear_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Bear GP', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle', display = display.none)
show_day_gp_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Day GP', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle2', display = display.none)
show_week_gp_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Week GP', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle2b', display = display.none)
show_month_gp_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Month GP', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle2b', display = display.none)
show_ext_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Ext.', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle2b', tooltip = 'Show a small \'Ex.\' marker at the bottom-left of every GP extension box (chart, overlay TFs, and persistent Day/Week/Month). Helps distinguish extensions from primary GPs at a glance.', display = display.none)
show_volume_stars = input.bool(true, title = '★ Volume Stars', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_toggle2', display = display.none)
use_emoji = input.bool(false, title = 'Emoji Labels', group = visualGroup, tooltip = 'Use 🐂/🐻 emoji instead of Bull/Bear text in GP box labels. Emoji may be hard to read on some color schemes.', display = display.none)
use_short_labels = input.bool(false, title = 'Shorthand Labels', group = visualGroup, tooltip = 'Replace verbose label text with compact shorthand wherever the active label toggles are showing something. Affects Bull/Bear GP box labels, Day/Week/Month GP box labels, and confluence labels.\n\nMapping:\n• Bull GP → BL, Bear GP → BR\n• Day GP → D, Week GP → W, Month GP → M\n\nConfluence tokens (composite labels):\n• Day/Week/Month GP → D / W / M\n• Ext → X, Day/Week/Month Ext → DX / WX / MX\n• GP and S/D unchanged (already short)\n• Joiner: + (no spaces)\n\nExample: "Week GP + Month GP + Week Ext + Month Ext" → "W+M+WX+MX".\n\nDoes not apply to emoji labels (🐂/🐻 stay as-is when Emoji Labels is on) or to the \'Ex.\' marker on extension boxes (already shorthand). Off by default.', display = display.none)

// Map a confluence-label token (the per-zone name pushed into _gpAllNames /
// _extAllNames) to its shorthand form when Shorthand Labels is on. Tokens
// here differ from box labels: confluence uses generic 'GP' / 'Ext' for
// chart-TF zones rather than Bull/Bear, since the box position itself
// disambiguates direction.
shortToken(string s) =>
    s == 'Day GP' ? 'D' : s == 'Week GP' ? 'W' : s == 'Month GP' ? 'M' : s == 'Ext' ? 'X' : s == 'Day Ext' ? 'DX' : s == 'Week Ext' ? 'WX' : s == 'Month Ext' ? 'MX' : s

// True when the confluence-label token names a persistent (Day/Week/Month) zone,
// main or extension. Used by the confluence detector to suppress persistent-vs-
// persistent overlaps — those boxes live at fixed right-side positions and their
// stacking is already visually obvious, so confluence boxes spanning the chart
// would just clutter without adding information.
isPersistentName(string s) =>
    s == 'Day GP' or s == 'Week GP' or s == 'Month GP' or s == 'Day Ext' or s == 'Week Ext' or s == 'Month Ext'
label_text_color = input.color(color.white, title = 'Label Color', group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_txt', display = display.none)
label_text_opacity = input.int(0, title = 'Opacity %', minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = visualGroup, inline = 'lbl_txt', tooltip = 'Color and transparency of GP box label text. 0 = fully opaque, 100 = fully transparent.', display = display.none)
box_border_style = input.string('Dashed', title = 'Border Style', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = visualGroup, tooltip = 'Visual style for the GP box borders.', display = display.none)
show_mid = input.bool(true, title = 'Midpoint Line', group = visualGroup, inline = '1', display = display.none)
mid_color = input.color(color.new(#4169E1, 30), title = '', group = visualGroup, inline = '1', display = display.none)
mid_line_style = input.string('Dotted', title = '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = visualGroup, inline = '1', display = display.none)
extend_mid_to_pivot = input.bool(false, title = 'Extend Midpoint to Pivot', group = visualGroup, tooltip = 'When enabled, the midpoint line extends backward from the active GP box to the originating pivot bar. Useful as a persistent visual anchor back to the zone origin.\n\nWhen disabled (default), the midpoint line stays inside the box, trailing with it.', display = display.none)
mid_extend_right = input.bool(false, title = 'Extend Midpoint Right', group = visualGroup, tooltip = 'Extend the midpoint (0.5 equilibrium) line indefinitely to the right past the GP box edge. Projects the equilibrium as a forward price reference — useful for tracking where price needs to return to reach the midpoint of the swing. Pairs with Extend Midpoint to Pivot for a full left-to-right equilibrium line.', display = display.none)
show_gp_anchor = input.bool(false, title = 'Show GP Anchor Dot', group = visualGroup, tooltip = 'Draw a small yellow dot at the pivot bar that originated each active GP. Useful if you want to see exactly where the zone is calculated from. Off by default to keep the chart clean.', display = display.none)

_borderStyle = box_border_style == 'Dashed' ? line.style_dashed : box_border_style == 'Dotted' ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
_fibStyle = line_style == 'Dashed' ? line.style_dashed : line_style == 'Dotted' ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
_midStyle = mid_line_style == 'Dashed' ? line.style_dashed : mid_line_style == 'Dotted' ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
_labelTextColor = color.new(label_text_color, label_text_opacity)

ladderGroup = '=== Fib Ladder ==='
show_ladder = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable Fib Ladder', group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Project a set of fib rungs from the chosen GP\'s pivot pair. Replaces generic fib retracement drawings with rungs that slide and disappear with their owning GP.', display = display.none)
ladder_mode = input.string('Retracement', title = 'Mode', options = ['Retracement', 'Extension', 'Both'], group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Retracement: rungs sit between the H–L range (pullback levels). Extension: rungs project beyond the pivot pair in the trend direction (target levels). Both: draw retracement rungs INSIDE the box and extension rungs OUTSIDE the box from the same pivot pair — a complete fib map at one anchor.', display = display.none)
ladder_source = input.string('Auto (most recent GP)', title = 'Source', options = ['All slots', 'Auto (most recent GP)', 'Pin: Chart P1', 'Pin: Chart P2', 'Pin: TF1', 'Pin: TF2', 'Pin: TF3', 'Pin: Day', 'Pin: Week', 'Pin: Month'], group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'All slots: every active GP draws its own ladder (can clutter — use sparingly). Auto: only the most recently formed GP shows a ladder, swapping live as new pivots print. Pin: lock the ladder to one source — chart profile slot, an overlay TF, or a persistent period.', display = display.none)
ladder_extension = input.string('Match GP', title = 'Rung Extension', options = ['Match GP', 'Extend Right', 'Extend Both Ways', 'Show on Closed GPs'], group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Match GP: rungs share the active GP\'s width and position — cleanest visual, default. Extend Right: rungs project past the right edge for forward planning. Extend Both Ways: rungs span the full chart so you can see how price has historically reacted to those exact levels. Show on Closed GPs: rungs stay matched to GP width but persist after the GP archives, leaving a faint trail of past ladders (capped at ~30 per slot for performance).', display = display.none)
ladder_lock = input.bool(true, title = 'Lock Levels', group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'When ON (default), each rung\'s price is anchored to the H/L from the moment its GP was drawn and only reprices when that GP itself redraws. Bull rungs lock to the pivot-high event; bear rungs lock to the pivot-low event — so opposing swings can\'t shift your targets.\n\nFor Day/Week/Month GPs the levels lock to the completed prior period\'s H/L from bar 1 of the new period (e.g. today\'s ladder uses yesterday\'s full range). Falls back to the current developing range when no prior period has completed.\n\nWhen OFF, all rungs recalculate continuously from the live H/L — useful if you specifically want the ladder to reflect the evolving range.', display = display.none)
ladder_levels = input.string('0.382, 0.5, 0.618, 0.786', title = 'Retracement Rungs', group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Comma-separated retracement levels (0–1). Drawn from H toward L on the bull side and from L toward H on the bear side.', display = display.none)
ladder_ext_levels = input.string('1.272, 1.414, 1.618, 2.0', title = 'Extension Rungs', group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Comma-separated extension levels (>1). 1.272 = classic minor target, 1.618 = golden, 2.0 = full measured move.', display = display.none)
ladder_ret_palette = input.string('Spectrum (ROYGBIV)', title = 'Retracement Palette', options = ['Spectrum (ROYGBIV)', 'Heatmap', 'Cool', 'Mono Gradient', 'Inherit GP Color', 'Custom Solid'], group = ladderGroup, inline = 'retpal', tooltip = 'Spectrum: per-rung rainbow so each level is visually distinct at a glance. Heatmap: red→orange→yellow (warm, danger-zone feel for deep pullbacks). Cool: blue→teal→green (calm, good for shallow pullbacks). Mono Gradient: symmetric fade from picked color (full strength at center rung, lighter at outer rungs). Inherit GP Color: all rungs share the owning GP\'s color. Custom Solid: all rungs share the picked color.', display = display.none)
ladder_ret_color = input.color(color.new(#FF69B4, 0), title = '', group = ladderGroup, inline = 'retpal', display = display.none)
ladder_ext_palette = input.string('Heatmap', title = 'Extension Palette', options = ['Spectrum (ROYGBIV)', 'Heatmap', 'Cool', 'Mono Gradient', 'Inherit GP Color', 'Custom Solid'], group = ladderGroup, inline = 'extpal', tooltip = 'Same options as Retracement Palette. Defaults to Heatmap for warm-toned extension targets. Pair with a Cool retracement palette for instant visual separation between pullback levels (inside box) and target levels (outside box).', display = display.none)
ladder_ext_color = input.color(color.new(#40E0D0, 0), title = '', group = ladderGroup, inline = 'extpal', display = display.none)
ladder_style = input.string('Dashed', title = 'Rung Style', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = ladderGroup, display = display.none)
ladder_show_labels = input.bool(false, title = 'Show Rung Labels', group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Annotate each rung with its fib level, price, or both. Labels sit offset to the side of the rung with a thin dashed connector — keeps the active zone clear while still naming every level. Toggle off for a pure-rung minimalist look.', display = display.none)
ladder_label_content = input.string('Level', title = 'Label Content', options = ['Level', 'Price', 'Both'], group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Level: "0.618". Price: "42153.50" (formatted to symbol mintick). Both: "0.618 @ 42153.50".', display = display.none)
ladder_label_side = input.string('Right', title = 'Label Side', options = ['Left', 'Right'], group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Which side of the rung the labels sit on. Right is recommended (forward-looking, doesn\'t clash with historical price action). Left can be useful when the GP sits at the right edge of the chart and right-side labels would be cropped.', display = display.none)
ladder_label_offset = input.int(5, title = 'Label Offset (bars)', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'How many bars the label sits away from the rung edge. The dashed connector spans this gap.', display = display.none)
ladder_label_color_mode = input.string('Match Rung', title = 'Label Color', options = ['Match Rung', 'Custom'], group = ladderGroup, inline = 'lblcol', tooltip = 'Match Rung: each label (and its connector) inherits the rung\'s palette color — strongest visual link between line and label. Custom: all labels use the picked color, useful when the palette has too much variety to read at a glance.', display = display.none)
ladder_label_color = input.color(color.new(color.white, 0), title = '', group = ladderGroup, inline = 'lblcol', display = display.none)
ladder_fill_between = input.bool(false, title = 'Fill Between Rungs', group = ladderGroup, tooltip = 'Shade the band between each pair of adjacent rungs. Color inherits from each rung\'s palette at reduced opacity. Works for all modes.', display = display.none)

_ladderStyle = ladder_style == 'Dashed' ? line.style_dashed : ladder_style == 'Dotted' ? line.style_dotted : line.style_solid
_ladderExtendLR = ladder_extension == 'Extend Right' ? extend.right : ladder_extension == 'Extend Both Ways' ? extend.both : extend.none
_ladderArchive = ladder_extension == 'Show on Closed GPs'
_ladderLabelOnLeft = ladder_label_side == 'Left'
_ladderLabelStyle = _ladderLabelOnLeft ? label.style_label_right : label.style_label_left

// Format a rung label according to user's content choice
formatRungLabel(string content, float level, float price) =>
    string _out = ''
    if content == 'Level'
        _out := str.tostring(level)
    else if content == 'Price'
        _out := str.tostring(price, format.mintick)
    else
        _out := str.tostring(level) + ' @ ' + str.tostring(price, format.mintick)
    _out

// Parse comma-separated rung levels into a float array
parseRungs(string s) =>
    arr = array.new_float()
    if not na(s) and str.length(s) > 0
        parts = str.split(s, ',')
        for i = 0 to array.size(parts) - 1
            v = str.tonumber(str.replace_all(array.get(parts, i), ' ', ''))
            if not na(v)
                array.push(arr, v)
    arr

_ladderRetRungs = parseRungs(ladder_levels)
_ladderExtRungs = parseRungs(ladder_ext_levels)

// ROYGBIV stops — fixed 7-color palette
var _roygbiv = array.from(color.red, color.orange, color.yellow, color.green, color.blue, #4B0082, #9400D3)
_heatStart = color.red
_heatEnd = color.yellow
_coolStart = color.blue
_coolEnd = color.green

// Resolve a rung color given palette mode, picked color, slot color, rung index, rung total
paletteColor(string palette, color picked, color slotColor, int idx, int total) =>
    color _out = na
    if palette == 'Inherit GP Color'
        _out := color.new(slotColor, 30)
    else if palette == 'Custom Solid'
        _out := picked
    else if palette == 'Spectrum (ROYGBIV)'
        // Distribute `total` rungs across the 7 stops as evenly as possible
        _stop = total <= 1 ? 0 : math.min(6, int(math.round(idx * 6.0 / math.max(1, total - 1))))
        _out := array.get(_roygbiv, _stop)
    else if palette == 'Heatmap'
        _t = total <= 1 ? 0.0 : idx / (total - 1.0)
        _out := color.from_gradient(_t, 0.0, 1.0, _heatStart, _heatEnd)
    else if palette == 'Cool'
        _t = total <= 1 ? 0.0 : idx / (total - 1.0)
        _out := color.from_gradient(_t, 0.0, 1.0, _coolStart, _coolEnd)
    else  // Mono Gradient — symmetric fade from picked (center) to lighter (outer)
        _center = (total - 1) / 2.0
        _maxDist = math.max(_center, 0.5)
        _dist = math.abs(idx - _center)
        _t = _dist / _maxDist
        _out := color.from_gradient(_t, 0.0, 1.0, picked, color.new(picked, 80))
    _out

// Auto-mode tracker: one-element array holds the slot id of the most recently
// changed GP. Array (vs plain var string) so manageLadder can mutate it from
// inside the function — Pine v6 forbids reassigning script-scope vars in functions.
var array<string> _ladderWinner = array.from('')

// Per-slot archive cap when "Show on Closed GPs" is active. Keeps line budget bounded.
ladderArchiveCap = 30

// Small object-list utilities used by the ladder manager.
clearLines(array<line> _a) =>
    while array.size(_a) > 0
        line.delete(array.pop(_a))
clearLabels(array<label> _a) =>
    while array.size(_a) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(_a))
clearFills(array<linefill> _a) =>
    while array.size(_a) > 0
        linefill.delete(array.pop(_a))
archiveLines(array<line> _from, array<line> _to) =>
    while array.size(_from) > 0
        array.push(_to, array.shift(_from))

// Sync one rung set (lines + labels + connectors + inter-rung fills) to its
// target count, position, palette, and label text. Pure — all object arrays
// are owned by the caller. Geometry:
//   retracement: y = base − sign · range · level
//   extension:   y = base + sign · range · (level − 1)
// with sign +1 for bull (base = swing high) and −1 for bear (base = swing low).
syncRungs(array<line> _rungs, array<label> _lbls, array<line> _cons, array<linefill> _fills, array<float> _levels, int _target, float _base, float _range, int _sign, bool _isExt, string _palette, color _picked, color _slotColor, int _leftBar, int _rightBar, int _labelBar, int _conStart, bool _showLblIn) =>
    while array.size(_rungs) > _target
        line.delete(array.pop(_rungs))
        if array.size(_lbls) > 0
            label.delete(array.pop(_lbls))
        if array.size(_cons) > 0
            line.delete(array.pop(_cons))
    while array.size(_rungs) < _target
        array.push(_rungs, line.new(_leftBar, 0.0, _rightBar, 0.0, style = _ladderStyle, extend = _ladderExtendLR))
        array.push(_lbls, label.new(0, 0.0, '', xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(color.black, 100), textcolor = color.white, style = _ladderLabelStyle, size = size.tiny))
        array.push(_cons, line.new(0, 0.0, 0, 0.0, style = line.style_dashed))
    _showRungLbl = _showLblIn and _target > 0
    _total = array.size(_levels)
    if _target > 0
        for i = 0 to _target - 1
            _lvl = array.get(_levels, i)
            _y = _isExt ? _base + _sign * _range * (_lvl - 1) : _base - _sign * _range * _lvl
            _col = paletteColor(_palette, _picked, _slotColor, i, _total)
            _ln = array.get(_rungs, i)
            line.set_xy1(_ln, _leftBar, _y)
            line.set_xy2(_ln, _rightBar, _y)
            line.set_color(_ln, _col)
            line.set_style(_ln, _ladderStyle)
            line.set_extend(_ln, _ladderExtendLR)
            _lblCol = ladder_label_color_mode == 'Match Rung' ? _col : ladder_label_color
            _lb = array.get(_lbls, i)
            label.set_xy(_lb, _labelBar, _y)
            label.set_text(_lb, _showRungLbl ? formatRungLabel(ladder_label_content, _lvl, _y) : '')
            label.set_textcolor(_lb, _showRungLbl ? _lblCol : color.new(color.black, 100))
            label.set_style(_lb, _ladderLabelStyle)
            _cn = array.get(_cons, i)
            line.set_xy1(_cn, _conStart, _y)
            line.set_xy2(_cn, _labelBar, _y)
            line.set_color(_cn, _showRungLbl ? _lblCol : color.new(color.black, 100))
    _fillTarget = ladder_fill_between and _target >= 2 ? _target - 1 : 0
    while array.size(_fills) > _fillTarget
        linefill.delete(array.pop(_fills))
    while array.size(_fills) < _fillTarget
        _fi = array.size(_fills)
        array.push(_fills, linefill.new(array.get(_rungs, _fi), array.get(_rungs, _fi + 1), color.new(color.white, 90)))
    if _fillTarget > 0
        for fi = 0 to _fillTarget - 1
            _fcol = paletteColor(_palette, _picked, _slotColor, fi, _total)
            linefill.set_color(array.get(_fills, fi), color.new(_fcol, 75))

// Ladder manager — call once per GP slot. var arrays scope per call site, so each
// invocation maintains its own bull/bear active + archived rung lists. Visibility,
// palette, extension, and archive logic all happen here so call sites stay one-line.
manageLadder(string slotId, string pinId, bool gpChanged, bool bullChanged, bool bearChanged, bool usePrevPeriod, bool hasBull, bool hasBear, float H, float L, color slotColor) =>
    // Active rung lines for the current pivot pair (cleared and rebuilt on gpChanged)
    var array<line> _bullRet = array.new_line()
    var array<line> _bearRet = array.new_line()
    var array<line> _bullExt = array.new_line()
    var array<line> _bearExt = array.new_line()
    // Per-rung label + dashed connector line. Synced 1:1 with their rung array.
    var array<label> _bullRetLbl = array.new_label()
    var array<label> _bearRetLbl = array.new_label()
    var array<label> _bullExtLbl = array.new_label()
    var array<label> _bearExtLbl = array.new_label()
    var array<line> _bullRetCon = array.new_line()
    var array<line> _bearRetCon = array.new_line()
    var array<line> _bullExtCon = array.new_line()
    var array<line> _bearExtCon = array.new_line()
    // Frozen archive of past pivot-pair ladders (only populated when ladder_extension = 'Show on Closed GPs')
    var array<line> _archive = array.new_line()
    // Inter-rung fill objects (cleared and rebuilt on gpChanged; never archived)
    var array<linefill> _bullRetFill = array.new_linefill()
    var array<linefill> _bearRetFill = array.new_linefill()
    var array<linefill> _bullExtFill = array.new_linefill()
    var array<linefill> _bearExtFill = array.new_linefill()
    // Per-side locked H/L: bull anchors to the pivot-high event, bear to the pivot-low event.
    // For persistent GPs (usePrevPeriod = true) the capture uses H[1]/L[1] at the period
    // boundary, giving the completed prior period's full range.
    var float _frozenBullH = na
    var float _frozenBullL = na
    var float _frozenBearH = na
    var float _frozenBearL = na
    _capH = usePrevPeriod ? H[1] : H
    _capL = usePrevPeriod ? L[1] : L
    _validCap = not na(_capH) and not na(_capL) and _capH > _capL
    if bullChanged and _validCap
        _frozenBullH := _capH
        _frozenBullL := _capL
    else if na(_frozenBullH) and not na(H) and not na(L) and H > L
        _frozenBullH := H
        _frozenBullL := L
    if bearChanged and _validCap
        _frozenBearH := _capH
        _frozenBearL := _capL
    else if na(_frozenBearH) and not na(H) and not na(L) and H > L
        _frozenBearH := H
        _frozenBearL := L

    if gpChanged and ladder_source == 'Auto (most recent GP)'
        array.set(_ladderWinner, 0, slotId)

    _visible = show_ladder and (ladder_source == 'All slots' or (ladder_source == 'Auto (most recent GP)' and array.get(_ladderWinner, 0) == slotId) or ladder_source == 'Pin: ' + pinId)

    _drawRet = ladder_mode == 'Retracement' or ladder_mode == 'Both'
    _drawExt = ladder_mode == 'Extension' or ladder_mode == 'Both'
    _retRungs = _ladderRetRungs
    _extRungs = _ladderExtRungs
    _retN = array.size(_retRungs)
    _extN = array.size(_extRungs)
    _leftBar = bar_index - gp_left_offset
    _rightBar = _ladderExtendLR != extend.none ? bar_index : bar_index + gp_right_offset
    _useH_bull = ladder_lock and not na(_frozenBullH) ? _frozenBullH : H
    _useL_bull = ladder_lock and not na(_frozenBullL) ? _frozenBullL : L
    _useH_bear = ladder_lock and not na(_frozenBearH) ? _frozenBearH : H
    _useL_bear = ladder_lock and not na(_frozenBearL) ? _frozenBearL : L
    _rangeBull = na(_useH_bull) or na(_useL_bull) ? 0.0 : _useH_bull - _useL_bull
    _rangeBear = na(_useH_bear) or na(_useL_bear) ? 0.0 : _useH_bear - _useL_bear

    _bullActive = _visible and hasBull and _rangeBull > 0
    _bearActive = _visible and hasBear and _rangeBear > 0

    _labelBar = _ladderLabelOnLeft ? _leftBar - ladder_label_offset : _rightBar + ladder_label_offset
    _conStart = _ladderLabelOnLeft ? _leftBar : _rightBar
    _showLbl = ladder_show_labels

    // On a fresh pivot pair, retire the old rungs before drawing new ones —
    // either freeze them into the archive (with cap trim) or delete outright.
    // On a fresh pivot pair, retire the old rungs before drawing new ones —
    // either freeze them into the archive (with cap trim) or delete outright.
    // Labels, connectors, and fills are always cleared (never archived) to
    // keep the chart readable and the label budget bounded.
    if gpChanged
        if _ladderArchive
            archiveLines(_bullRet, _archive)
            archiveLines(_bearRet, _archive)
            archiveLines(_bullExt, _archive)
            archiveLines(_bearExt, _archive)
            while array.size(_archive) > ladderArchiveCap
                line.delete(array.shift(_archive))
        else
            clearLines(_bullRet)
            clearLines(_bearRet)
            clearLines(_bullExt)
            clearLines(_bearExt)
        clearLabels(_bullRetLbl)
        clearLabels(_bearRetLbl)
        clearLabels(_bullExtLbl)
        clearLabels(_bearExtLbl)
        clearLines(_bullRetCon)
        clearLines(_bearRetCon)
        clearLines(_bullExtCon)
        clearLines(_bearExtCon)
        clearFills(_bullRetFill)
        clearFills(_bearRetFill)
        clearFills(_bullExtFill)
        clearFills(_bearExtFill)

    // Sync all four rung sets (bull/bear x retracement/extension) — geometry
    // and palette differ per set; syncRungs does the object bookkeeping.
    syncRungs(_bullRet, _bullRetLbl, _bullRetCon, _bullRetFill, _retRungs, _bullActive and _drawRet ? _retN : 0, _useH_bull, _rangeBull, 1, false, ladder_ret_palette, ladder_ret_color, slotColor, _leftBar, _rightBar, _labelBar, _conStart, _showLbl)
    syncRungs(_bullExt, _bullExtLbl, _bullExtCon, _bullExtFill, _extRungs, _bullActive and _drawExt ? _extN : 0, _useH_bull, _rangeBull, 1, true, ladder_ext_palette, ladder_ext_color, slotColor, _leftBar, _rightBar, _labelBar, _conStart, _showLbl)
    syncRungs(_bearRet, _bearRetLbl, _bearRetCon, _bearRetFill, _retRungs, _bearActive and _drawRet ? _retN : 0, _useL_bear, _rangeBear, -1, false, ladder_ret_palette, ladder_ret_color, slotColor, _leftBar, _rightBar, _labelBar, _conStart, _showLbl)
    syncRungs(_bearExt, _bearExtLbl, _bearExtCon, _bearExtFill, _extRungs, _bearActive and _drawExt ? _extN : 0, _useL_bear, _rangeBear, -1, true, ladder_ext_palette, ladder_ext_color, slotColor, _leftBar, _rightBar, _labelBar, _conStart, _showLbl)

confluenceGroup = '=== Confluence & Alerts ==='
show_confluence = input.bool(true, title = 'Confluence Zones', group = confluenceGroup, tooltip = 'Highlight where zones overlap. Label shows the type: GP + GP, GP + S/D, Ext + Ext, Ext + GP, or Ext + S/D.\n\nPersistent-vs-persistent overlaps (Day/Week/Month boxes with each other) are suppressed — the overlap is already obvious from the fixed right-side boxes themselves.\n\nGP + GP needs more than one GP on the chart — enable TF1/TF2/TF3 in the Overlay sections for multi-timeframe stacks.', display = display.none)
show_confluence_label = input.bool(true, title = 'Confluence Label', group = confluenceGroup, tooltip = 'Show text on confluence boxes indicating the overlap type (\'GP + GP\', \'GP + S/D\', \'Ext + Ext\', \'Ext + GP\', or \'Ext + S/D\'). Turn off if you only want the highlight color.', display = display.none)
confluence_color = input.color(color.new(color.purple, 70), title = 'Confluence Color', group = confluenceGroup, tooltip = 'Color used for all confluence highlight boxes. Every type shares this color — the label text tells you which is which.', display = display.none)
conf_score_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Strength Score', group = confluenceGroup, inline = 'confsc', tooltip = 'When three or more zones stack in the same price area, tag the highlight with how many agree (×3, ×4 …) and make its fill more solid the more zones pile up. Ordinary two-zone overlaps keep the normal color and label, so only the genuinely crowded areas stand out.', display = display.none)
conf_score_boost = input.int(12, title = 'Glow per Zone', minval = 0, maxval = 30, group = confluenceGroup, inline = 'confsc', tooltip = 'How much more solid the highlight becomes for each zone beyond the first two. 0 = the color never changes and only the ×N count is shown.', display = display.none)
show_persistent_sd_confluence = input.bool(false, title = 'Persistent GP × S/D Confluence', group = confluenceGroup, tooltip = 'When ON, confluence boxes are drawn where Day/Week/Month GPs (or their extensions) overlap S/D zones. Off by default — these overlaps tend to clutter the chart because the persistent boxes are large and frequently intersect S/D zones at low TFs.\n\nChart-TF GP × S/D and overlay TF GP × S/D are always enabled regardless of this setting.', display = display.none)
approach_on = input.bool(false, title = 'Approaching-Zone Alerts', group = confluenceGroup, inline = 'appr', tooltip = 'Fire an alert when price gets CLOSE to a zone, before it actually touches — an early heads-up so you can get ready instead of reacting late. "Close" is measured in ATR (a typical bar\'s range), so the warning distance adapts to how fast the market moves. Covers every GP, extension, and S/D zone on the chart.\n\nDelivered through the same alert stream as zone touches: create an alert with Condition set to "Any alert() function call". A matching "Approaching Any Zone" entry is also available in the Condition dropdown for targeted alerts.', display = display.none)
approach_atr = input.float(0.5, title = 'Within (ATR)', minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = confluenceGroup, inline = 'appr', tooltip = 'How close price must get to a zone edge to count as approaching, measured in ATR. 0.5 = half a typical bar\'s range away.', display = display.none)
alert_on = input.bool(true, title = 'All-Events Alert Stream', group = confluenceGroup, tooltip = 'When ON, every zone touch fires a detailed alert message with direction, timeframe, profile, and symbol.\n\nExamples:\n• "Bull 15 Intraday Golden Pocket Hit on BTCUSD"\n• "Bull 15 Intraday GP Extension Hit on BTCUSD"\n• "Day GP Hit on BTCUSD"\n• "Day GP Extension Hit on BTCUSD"\n• "Demand Zone Hit on BTCUSD"\n\nCovers: Bull/Bear GPs, Bull/Bear GP Extensions, Day/Week/Month GPs, Day/Week/Month GP Extensions, Demand zones, Supply zones.\n\nTo arm: right-click chart → Add alert → set Condition to this indicator → in the second dropdown choose "Any alert() function call".\n\nFor targeted alerts (e.g. only Bull GP Extension hits), leave this OFF and pick a specific Condition when creating an alert. The two modes can run side-by-side. Available conditions: Bull GP Touch, Bear GP Touch, Bull GP Extension Touch, Bear GP Extension Touch, Day GP Touch, Week GP Touch, Month GP Touch, Demand Zone Touch, Supply Zone Touch, Confluence Zone Touch, Any Zone Touch.', display = display.none)

dashGroup = '=== Zone Dashboard ==='
dash_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Show Zone Dashboard', group = dashGroup, tooltip = 'Compact corner table listing every active zone, sorted nearest-to-price first. Columns:\n\nZone — what it is (direction, timeframe, profile; Demand/Supply for S/D zones, ★ marks above-average volume).\nEdge — the price you\'d hit first (the zone\'s near edge, or its middle when price is inside).\nDist — how far away that edge is, in ATR (typical bar ranges). 0 = price is in the zone.\nWhere — the zone\'s position relative to price: Below = potential support, Above = potential resistance, Inside = price is in it right now.', display = display.none)
dash_pos = input.string('Top Right', title = 'Position', options = ['Top Right', 'Top Left', 'Bottom Right', 'Bottom Left', 'Middle Right'], group = dashGroup, inline = 'dash1', display = display.none)
dash_size = input.string('Small', title = 'Text', options = ['Tiny', 'Small', 'Normal'], group = dashGroup, inline = 'dash1', display = display.none)
dash_max = input.int(8, title = 'Max Rows', minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = dashGroup, inline = 'dash1', tooltip = 'How many zones to list. When there are more, the nearest ones win.', display = display.none)
dash_pad_x = input.int(0, title = 'Side Gap', minval = 0, maxval = 40, group = dashGroup, inline = 'dash2', tooltip = 'Pushes the dashboard away from the side edge of the chart, in character widths. Useful when something else lives at the right edge — like the Volume Strata histogram — and the table sits on top of it. Only visible with the Right (or Left) positions.', display = display.none)
dash_pad_y = input.int(0, title = 'Vertical Gap', minval = 0, maxval = 30, group = dashGroup, inline = 'dash2', tooltip = 'Pushes the dashboard down from the top (for Top positions) or up from the bottom (for the others), in blank rows.', display = display.none)
dash_stats = input.bool(true, title = 'Hit-Rate Rows', group = dashGroup, inline = 'dash3', tooltip = 'Add rows at the bottom of the dashboard showing how each pivot profile\'s Golden Pockets have performed on this chart. A zone counts as tested once price comes back into it; it then either holds (stays valid until a new swing replaces it) or fails (price pushes through and invalidates it). Shown as held/tested with a percentage — e.g. Swing GP · 21/34 · 62%.\n\nCounts build from the chart history that has been processed, so the sample grows with more bars and resets when settings change. Only the pivot profiles (Scalping / Intraday / Swing / Custom) are tracked — Quick and Day/Week/Month GPs don\'t use invalidation, so held vs failed isn\'t defined for them. Works best with Invalidate Active GP turned on; with it off, nothing can fail.', display = display.none)

maGroup = '=== MA Filter ==='
ma_filter = input.string('Off', title = 'Filter Mode', options = ['Off', 'Trend Direction', 'Price Position'], group = maGroup, tooltip = 'Off: Draw all GP boxes (Line Mode and Trend Direction Bias are ignored).\n\nTrend Direction: Combines with Line Mode to define trend.\n- Fast Line: trend comes from fast MA slope.\n- Both Lines: trend comes from fast vs slow relationship.\nThen Trend Direction Bias decides whether Bull GPs appear with the trend or against it.\n\nPrice Position: Combines with Line Mode to define required MA side at pivot.\n- Fast Line: pivots must be above/below fast MA only.\n- Both Lines: pivots must be above/below both fast and slow MAs.\n\nMAs are evaluated per timeframe slot, so each slot is filtered by its own TF-appropriate MA. The MA lines plotted below reflect the chart timeframe only.', display = display.none)
trend_dir_bias = input.string('With Trend', title = 'Trend Direction Bias', options = ['With Trend', 'Against Trend'], group = maGroup, tooltip = 'With Trend: Bull in uptrend, Bear in downtrend (default).\nAgainst Trend: Bull in downtrend, Bear in uptrend.', display = display.none)
ma_line_mode = input.string('Fast Line', title = 'Line Mode', options = ['Fast Line', 'Both Lines'], group = maGroup, tooltip = 'Used only when Filter Mode is Trend Direction or Price Position.\n\nFast Line combo:\n- Trend Direction: trend = fast MA slope.\n- Price Position: pivots must be above/below fast MA.\n\nBoth Lines combo:\n- Trend Direction: trend = fast MA above/below slow MA.\n- Price Position: pivots must be above/below both MAs.\n\nNo effect when Filter Mode = Off.', display = display.none)
ma_fast_type = input.string('EMA', title = 'Fast MA Type', options = ['SMA', 'EMA'], group = maGroup, inline = '1', display = display.none)
ma_fast_length = input.int(9, title = 'Length', group = maGroup, inline = '1', display = display.none)
ma_slow_type = input.string('EMA', title = 'Slow MA Type', options = ['SMA', 'EMA'], group = maGroup, inline = '2', display = display.none)
ma_slow_length = input.int(21, title = 'Length', group = maGroup, inline = '2', display = display.none)
ma_source = input.source(close, title = 'Source', group = maGroup, display = display.none)
show_ma_fast = input.bool(false, title = 'Show Fast MA', group = maGroup, inline = '3', display = display.none)
ma_fast_color = input.color(color.blue, title = '', group = maGroup, inline = '3', display = display.none)
ma_fast_linestyle_str = input.string('Solid', title = '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = maGroup, inline = '3', display = display.none)
show_ma_slow = input.bool(false, title = 'Show Slow MA', group = maGroup, inline = '4', display = display.none)
ma_slow_color = input.color(color.red, title = '', group = maGroup, inline = '4', display = display.none)
ma_slow_linestyle_str = input.string('Solid', title = '', options = ['Solid', 'Dashed', 'Dotted'], group = maGroup, inline = '4', display = display.none)
// Resolve string inputs to plot.linestyle_* constants (Pine, Sept 2025).
_maFastLineStyle = ma_fast_linestyle_str == 'Dashed' ? plot.linestyle_dashed : ma_fast_linestyle_str == 'Dotted' ? plot.linestyle_dotted : plot.linestyle_solid
_maSlowLineStyle = ma_slow_linestyle_str == 'Dashed' ? plot.linestyle_dashed : ma_slow_linestyle_str == 'Dotted' ? plot.linestyle_dotted : plot.linestyle_solid

sdGroup = '=== Supply / Demand Zones ==='
sd_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Enable S/D Zones', group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Draw supply and demand zones on the chart. A zone is placed when price makes a strong directional move, marking the last area where buyers or sellers were in control before that move.\n\nThe sensitivity profile is chosen from whichever overlay timeframe slot matches the current chart. If none match, Auto selects one based on chart timeframe.\n\nNote: S/D zones are not reliable on Heikin Ashi charts. HA modifies candle open and close values, which can cause extra zones to appear. GP zones are always unaffected.', display = display.none)
sd_atr_mult_in = input.float(1.0, title = 'ATR Multiplier', minval = 0.5, step = 0.1, group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Only used when the active S/D profile is Custom.\n\nMinimum candle body size as a multiple of ATR to qualify as an impulsive move. Higher = fewer but stronger zones.', display = display.none)
sd_lookback_in = input.int(10, title = 'Lookback', minval = 1, group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Only used when the active S/D profile is Custom.\n\nHow far back (in bars) to search for the order block — the last opposing candle before the impulse. If no opposing candle is found within this range, no zone is created.\n\nShort (3–5): Only catches order blocks right at the impulse. Best for scalping.\nMedium (8–10): General purpose. Used by Intraday and Swing presets.\nLong (15–20): Searches deeper into consolidation. May find stale order blocks.', display = display.none)
sd_retests_in = input.int(3, title = 'Max Retests', minval = 1, group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Only used when the active S/D profile is Custom.\n\nHow many times price can revisit a zone before it is considered used up. Each retest shrinks the zone — the tested edge moves inward by 1/N of the zone height, visually showing orders being absorbed. On the final retest the zone is removed.\n\nLower = zones shrink and disappear faster.', display = display.none)
sd_max_zones_in = input.int(5, title = 'Max Zones Per Side', minval = 1, group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Only used when the active S/D profile is Custom.\n\nMaximum number of active supply or demand zones shown at once. Oldest zones are removed first.', display = display.none)
sd_overlap_thresh = input.int(50, title = 'Overlap Threshold %', minval = 10, maxval = 90, group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'How much two same-side zones must overlap before they merge into one. The merged zone covers the combined range (capped by Max Zone Height) and inherits a ★ if either zone had one.\n\nLower (30–40%): More aggressive merging — fewer zones, less clutter. Better for low TFs where impulses cluster.\nDefault (50%): Balanced.\nHigher (60–80%): Permissive — keeps more nearby zones distinct. Better for high TFs where distinct levels matter.\n\nOnly used when the active S/D profile is Custom. Preset values: Scalping 40%, Intraday 50%, Swing 60%. See the S/D Profile dropdown (in each Overlay Timeframe section) for all preset values.', display = display.none)
sd_max_height_in = input.float(2.0, title = 'Max Zone Height (ATR)', minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Only used when the active S/D profile is Custom.\n\nMaximum zone height as a multiple of ATR. Zones taller than this are clamped toward the impulse candle. Prevents oversized zones during volatile consolidation periods.\n\nLower (1.0–1.5): Very tight zones, precise entries.\nDefault (2.0): Balanced.\nHigher (3.0+): Allows wider zones for swing levels.', display = display.none)
sd_bos = input.bool(true, title = 'Break of Structure', group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Only create an S/D zone when the impulse candle closes beyond recent structure — above the highest high (demand) or below the lowest low (supply) of the lookback window.\n\nThis filters out large candles that move within a range but don\'t actually shift market structure. The result is fewer, higher-quality zones at genuine turning points.\n\nDisable to allow any qualifying impulse candle to generate a zone, regardless of whether it broke structure.', display = display.none)
sd_confirm = input.bool(false, title = 'Confirm Zones on Bar Close', group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'When ON, S/D zones only form once the impulse candle has fully closed, so a zone never appears and then vanishes while the candle is still forming. Trades a little speed for stability — the zone shows up one bar later but then stays put.\n\nWhen OFF (default), zones appear immediately on the forming candle but can shift or disappear until that candle closes.', display = display.none)
sd_invalidate = input.bool(true, title = 'Remove Broken Zones', group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'When ON (default), a zone is removed once a candle closes through its far side — a demand zone goes when a candle closes below its bottom, a supply zone when one closes above its top. This clears away zones that price has already broken through instead of leaving them on the chart.\n\nWhen OFF, broken zones stay until the Max Zones Per Side limit pushes them off.', display = display.none)
sd_retest_close = input.bool(false, title = 'Retest on Bar Close', group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'When ON, a retest only counts when a candle closes into the zone — a quick wick that pokes in and pulls back without closing there won\'t shrink or use up the zone. More conservative, so zones last longer.\n\nWhen OFF (default), any wick into the zone counts as a retest.', display = display.none)
sd_show_labels = input.bool(true, title = 'Show S/D Labels', group = sdGroup, tooltip = 'Display Demand or Supply text labels on S/D zone boxes.', display = display.none)
sd_demand_color = input.color(color.new(color.green, 80), title = 'Demand', group = sdGroup, inline = 'sd_colors', display = display.none)
sd_supply_color = input.color(color.new(color.red, 80), title = 'Supply', group = sdGroup, inline = 'sd_colors', display = display.none)
sd_label_text_color = input.color(color.white, title = 'Label Color', group = sdGroup, inline = 'sd_lbl_txt', display = display.none)
sd_label_text_opacity = input.int(0, title = 'Opacity %', minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = sdGroup, inline = 'sd_lbl_txt', tooltip = 'Color and transparency of S/D zone label text. 0 = fully opaque, 100 = fully transparent.', display = display.none)
_sdLabelTextColor = color.new(sd_label_text_color, sd_label_text_opacity)

fvgGroup = '=== Fair Value Gaps ==='
fvg_on = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable FVG Zones', group = fvgGroup, tooltip = 'Draw Fair Value Gaps — the ICT three-candle imbalance. When a strong candle leaves a gap between the candle before it and the candle after it (their wicks never overlap), that strip of prices was never traded. Price often returns to these zones to rebalance before continuing, so a bullish FVG below price acts as support and a bearish FVG above price as resistance.\n\nGaps are only created once the third candle has closed, so they never appear and then vanish. FVGs feed the confluence detection, alerts, and dashboard just like GP and S/D zones — an FVG stacked inside a Golden Pocket is a classic high-interest area.', display = display.none)
fvg_min_atr = input.float(0.3, title = 'Min Gap Height (ATR)', minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = fvgGroup, inline = 'fvg1', tooltip = 'Ignore gaps smaller than this, measured in ATR (a typical bar\'s range). Filters out the many tiny gaps that appear on fast timeframes. 0 = keep every gap.', display = display.none)
fvg_max_zones = input.int(4, title = 'Max Per Side', minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = fvgGroup, inline = 'fvg1', tooltip = 'How many bullish and how many bearish FVGs to keep at once. Oldest are removed first.', display = display.none)
fvg_fill_rule = input.string('Fully Filled', title = 'Remove When', options = ['Fully Filled', 'Midpoint Touched'], group = fvgGroup, tooltip = 'When a gap counts as used up and is removed.\n\nFully Filled — price has traded through the entire gap.\nMidpoint Touched — price has reached the gap\'s original halfway point (the "consequent encroachment" level in ICT terms), which many traders treat as the gap being satisfied.', display = display.none)
fvg_shrink = input.bool(true, title = 'Shrink as Filled', group = fvgGroup, inline = 'fvg2', tooltip = 'Trim the zone as price partially fills it, so only the untraded remainder stays highlighted.', display = display.none)
fvg_show_labels = input.bool(true, title = 'Labels', group = fvgGroup, inline = 'fvg2', tooltip = 'Show an FVG label on each gap box (★ marks gaps whose displacement candle had above-average volume).', display = display.none)
fvg_bull_color = input.color(color.new(#00BCD4, 85), title = 'Bull', group = fvgGroup, inline = 'fvg3', display = display.none)
fvg_bear_color = input.color(color.new(#E91E63, 85), title = 'Bear', group = fvgGroup, inline = 'fvg3', display = display.none)

// Resolve S/D profile
autoSDProfile(_tf) =>
    _seconds = _tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(_tf)
    _minutes = _seconds / 60
    _minutes <= 5 ? 'Scalping' : _minutes <= 30 ? 'Intraday' : 'Swing'

resolveSdProfile(_slotProfile, _tf) =>
    _slotProfile == 'Auto' ? autoSDProfile(_tf) : _slotProfile

volGroup = '=== Volume Enhancement ==='
vol_enhance_on = input.bool(true, title = 'Enable', group = volGroup, tooltip = 'Visually highlight GP and S/D zones that formed on above-average volume. High-volume zones are more opaque and marked with a ★ in the label.\n\nWhy it matters: Zones backed by strong volume are more likely to hold — they represent real buying or selling pressure, not just thin price swings.', display = display.none)
vol_ma_len = input.int(21, title = 'Volume MA Length', minval = 1, group = volGroup, tooltip = 'Length of the volume moving average used to determine what counts as above-average volume. A bar with volume exceeding this MA is considered high-volume.\n\nLower (10–15): More sensitive, more zones flagged.\nDefault (21): Balanced.\nHigher (30–50): Only flags truly exceptional volume bars.', display = display.none)
vol_transp_boost = input.int(20, title = 'Opacity Boost', minval = 5, maxval = 80, group = volGroup, tooltip = 'How much more visible high-volume zones become. This reduces the transparency of the zone box.\n\nExample: If a GP box is normally at 80% transparent and boost is 20, a volume-confirmed GP box becomes 60% transparent.\n\nHigher = more contrast between normal and high-volume zones.', display = display.none)

tf1Group = '=== Overlay Timeframe 1 ==='
tf1_on = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable', group = tf1Group, inline = '0', tooltip = 'Draw GPs from another timeframe overlaid onto the current chart. Each overlay slot has its own timeframe, color, and set of profile checkboxes. Leave all slots disabled if you only want chart-timeframe GPs.', display = display.none)
tf1_tf = input.timeframe('', title = '', group = tf1Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf1_box_color = input.color(color.new(#9370DB, 80), title = '', group = tf1Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf1_piv_distance = input.int(3, title = 'Pivot Distance (Custom only)', group = tf1Group, tooltip = 'Only used when Show Custom is ticked for this slot.\n\nBars left/right to confirm a pivot.\n\nConfirmation delay = pivot distance × bar length.\nExample: distance 3 on a 5 min chart = 15 min delay.\nLower for faster scalp signals (more noise), higher for stronger zones.\n\nSuggested values:\n• 1–5 min: 2–4\n• 6–30 min: 5–8\n• 1H–4H: 8–15\n• Daily+: 10–20', display = display.none)
tf1_show_scalping = input.bool(false, title = 'Scalping', group = tf1Group, inline = 'tf1_gp', tooltip = 'Tick one or more profiles to draw on this overlay timeframe. Each profile tuned with its own pivot-distance preset. Custom uses the Pivot Distance input above.', display = display.none)
tf1_show_intraday = input.bool(false, title = 'Intraday', group = tf1Group, inline = 'tf1_gp', display = display.none)
tf1_show_swing = input.bool(false, title = 'Swing', group = tf1Group, inline = 'tf1_gp', display = display.none)
tf1_show_custom = input.bool(false, title = 'Custom', group = tf1Group, inline = 'tf1_gp', display = display.none)
tf1_show_quick = input.bool(false, title = 'Quick', group = tf1Group, inline = 'tf1_gp2', tooltip = 'Draw a Quick GP from this timeframe — a zone taken straight from the highest and lowest price over a set number of recent bars, without waiting for a swing to confirm. The bar count is set by Quick Profile Lookback in the Chart GPs section.', display = display.none)
tf1_sd_profile = input.string('Off', title = 'S/D Profile', options = ['Off', 'Auto', 'Scalping', 'Intraday', 'Swing', 'Custom'], group = tf1Group, tooltip = 'S/D profile used when this slot\'s timeframe matches the chart timeframe. S/D zones are always drawn from chart data, not the slot\'s timeframe.\n\nOff — Suppresses S/D drawing entirely while this slot is the matched slot for the chart timeframe. Use this if you want this slot for GP overlay only and don\'t want S/D to appear on the chart.\n\nAuto picks by chart TF:\n• ≤5 min → Scalping\n• ≤30 min → Intraday\n• >30 min → Swing\n\nPreset values (ATR Mult / Lookback / Retests / Max Zones / Overlap % / Max Height ATR):\n• Scalping:  1.0 / 5  / 3 / 3 / 40% / 1.5\n• Intraday:  1.0 / 10 / 3 / 5 / 50% / 1.5\n• Swing:     1.0 / 10 / 3 / 5 / 60% / 2.0\n• Custom:    uses the values set in the S/D Zones section above.\n\nBreak of Structure, Volume Confirmation, and the extinction rules (break behavior, retest count) always come from the S/D Zones section regardless of profile.', display = display.none)

tf2Group = '=== Overlay Timeframe 2 ==='
tf2_on = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable', group = tf2Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf2_tf = input.timeframe('240', title = '', group = tf2Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf2_box_color = input.color(color.new(#00BFFF, 80), title = '', group = tf2Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf2_piv_distance = input.int(5, title = 'Pivot Distance (Custom only)', group = tf2Group, tooltip = 'See Pivot Distance in Overlay Timeframe 1.', display = display.none)
tf2_show_scalping = input.bool(false, title = 'Scalping', group = tf2Group, inline = 'tf2_gp', display = display.none)
tf2_show_intraday = input.bool(false, title = 'Intraday', group = tf2Group, inline = 'tf2_gp', display = display.none)
tf2_show_swing = input.bool(false, title = 'Swing', group = tf2Group, inline = 'tf2_gp', display = display.none)
tf2_show_custom = input.bool(false, title = 'Custom', group = tf2Group, inline = 'tf2_gp', display = display.none)
tf2_show_quick = input.bool(false, title = 'Quick', group = tf2Group, inline = 'tf2_gp2', tooltip = 'See Quick in Overlay Timeframe 1.', display = display.none)
tf2_sd_profile = input.string('Off', title = 'S/D Profile', options = ['Off', 'Auto', 'Scalping', 'Intraday', 'Swing', 'Custom'], group = tf2Group, tooltip = 'See S/D Profile in Overlay Timeframe 1.', display = display.none)

tf3Group = '=== Overlay Timeframe 3 ==='
tf3_on = input.bool(false, title = 'Enable', group = tf3Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf3_tf = input.timeframe('D', title = '', group = tf3Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf3_box_color = input.color(color.new(#FF6347, 80), title = '', group = tf3Group, inline = '0', display = display.none)
tf3_piv_distance = input.int(5, title = 'Pivot Distance (Custom only)', group = tf3Group, tooltip = 'See Pivot Distance in Overlay Timeframe 1.', display = display.none)
tf3_show_scalping = input.bool(false, title = 'Scalping', group = tf3Group, inline = 'tf3_gp', display = display.none)
tf3_show_intraday = input.bool(false, title = 'Intraday', group = tf3Group, inline = 'tf3_gp', display = display.none)
tf3_show_swing = input.bool(false, title = 'Swing', group = tf3Group, inline = 'tf3_gp', display = display.none)
tf3_show_custom = input.bool(false, title = 'Custom', group = tf3Group, inline = 'tf3_gp', display = display.none)
tf3_show_quick = input.bool(false, title = 'Quick', group = tf3Group, inline = 'tf3_gp2', tooltip = 'See Quick in Overlay Timeframe 1.', display = display.none)
tf3_sd_profile = input.string('Off', title = 'S/D Profile', options = ['Off', 'Auto', 'Scalping', 'Intraday', 'Swing', 'Custom'], group = tf3Group, tooltip = 'See S/D Profile in Overlay Timeframe 1.', display = display.none)

// Resolve GP profile
autoGPProfile(_tf) =>
    _seconds = _tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(_tf)
    _minutes = _seconds / 60
    _minutes <= 5 ? 'Scalping' : _minutes <= 30 ? 'Intraday' : 'Swing'

profilePivot(_tf, _profile) =>
    _seconds = _tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(_tf)
    _minutes = _seconds / 60
    if _profile == 'Scalping'
        _minutes <= 5 ? 2 : _minutes <= 30 ? 4 : _minutes <= 240 ? 6 : 8
    else if _profile == 'Swing'
        _minutes <= 5 ? 5 : _minutes <= 30 ? 8 : _minutes <= 240 ? 15 : 20
    else  // Intraday
        _minutes <= 5 ? 3 : _minutes <= 30 ? 6 : _minutes <= 240 ? 10 : 15

// Quick-profile lookback (bars) for a timeframe. 0 in the input means auto-size by TF;
// a positive input value forces that exact bar count on every Quick GP.
quickLen(_tf) =>
    _seconds = _tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(_tf)
    _minutes = _seconds / 60
    quick_lookback_in > 0 ? quick_lookback_in : (_minutes <= 5 ? 50 : _minutes <= 30 ? 40 : _minutes <= 240 ? 30 : 20)

// Quick range — highest high / lowest low over a lookback, the raw input to a Quick GP.
quickRange(_len, _hi, _lo) =>
    [ta.highest(_hi, _len), ta.lowest(_lo, _len)]

// Pretty-print a timeframe for a corner tag, e.g. '15' -> '15m', '60' -> '1h', 'D' -> '1D'.
// Empty input resolves to the chart timeframe.
prettyTF(_tf) =>
    _s = _tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(_tf)
    _s < 60 ? str.tostring(_s) + 's' : _s < 3600 ? str.tostring(int(_s / 60)) + 'm' : _s < 86400 ? str.tostring(int(_s / 3600)) + 'h' : _s < 604800 ? str.tostring(int(_s / 86400)) + 'D' : _s < 2592000 ? str.tostring(int(_s / 604800)) + 'W' : str.tostring(int(_s / 2592000)) + 'M'

// Resolve chart-TF profiles (Profile 1 may be Auto, Profile 2 is never Auto)
_chartP1 = chart_gp_profile_1 == 'Off' ? 'Off' : chart_gp_profile_1 == 'Auto' ? autoGPProfile('') : chart_gp_profile_1
_chartP2 = chart_gp_profile_2

chart_use_scalp = _chartP1 == 'Scalping' or _chartP2 == 'Scalping'
chart_use_intr = _chartP1 == 'Intraday' or _chartP2 == 'Intraday'
chart_use_swing = _chartP1 == 'Swing' or _chartP2 == 'Swing'
chart_use_quick = _chartP1 == 'Quick' or _chartP2 == 'Quick'

// Route color per profile: P1 wins if it owns the profile, otherwise P2's color
chart_color_scalp = _chartP1 == 'Scalping' ? chart_gp_box_color : chart_gp_box_color_2
chart_color_intr = _chartP1 == 'Intraday' ? chart_gp_box_color : chart_gp_box_color_2
chart_color_swing = _chartP1 == 'Swing' ? chart_gp_box_color : chart_gp_box_color_2
chart_color_quick = _chartP1 == 'Quick' ? chart_gp_box_color : chart_gp_box_color_2

// Ladder pin id per chart slot — same rule as color routing (P1 owns if profile matches)
chart_pin_scalp = _chartP1 == 'Scalping' ? 'Chart P1' : 'Chart P2'
chart_pin_intr = _chartP1 == 'Intraday' ? 'Chart P1' : 'Chart P2'
chart_pin_swing = _chartP1 == 'Swing' ? 'Chart P1' : 'Chart P2'
chart_pin_quick = _chartP1 == 'Quick' ? 'Chart P1' : 'Chart P2'

// Suppress overlay-slot profile checkboxes that duplicate chart profiles on the same TF
_chartSecForDedup = timeframe.in_seconds()
_tf1SecForDedup = tf1_tf == '' ? _chartSecForDedup : timeframe.in_seconds(tf1_tf)
_tf2SecForDedup = tf2_tf == '' ? _chartSecForDedup : timeframe.in_seconds(tf2_tf)
_tf3SecForDedup = tf3_tf == '' ? _chartSecForDedup : timeframe.in_seconds(tf3_tf)
_tf1OnChart = _tf1SecForDedup == _chartSecForDedup
_tf2OnChart = _tf2SecForDedup == _chartSecForDedup
_tf3OnChart = _tf3SecForDedup == _chartSecForDedup

tf1_gp_use_scalping = tf1_show_scalping and not (_tf1OnChart and chart_use_scalp)
tf1_gp_use_intraday = tf1_show_intraday and not (_tf1OnChart and chart_use_intr)
tf1_gp_use_swing = tf1_show_swing and not (_tf1OnChart and chart_use_swing)
tf1_gp_use_custom = tf1_show_custom
tf1_gp_use_quick = tf1_show_quick and not (_tf1OnChart and chart_use_quick)

tf2_gp_use_scalping = tf2_show_scalping and not (_tf2OnChart and chart_use_scalp)
tf2_gp_use_intraday = tf2_show_intraday and not (_tf2OnChart and chart_use_intr)
tf2_gp_use_swing = tf2_show_swing and not (_tf2OnChart and chart_use_swing)
tf2_gp_use_custom = tf2_show_custom
tf2_gp_use_quick = tf2_show_quick and not (_tf2OnChart and chart_use_quick)

tf3_gp_use_scalping = tf3_show_scalping and not (_tf3OnChart and chart_use_scalp)
tf3_gp_use_intraday = tf3_show_intraday and not (_tf3OnChart and chart_use_intr)
tf3_gp_use_swing = tf3_show_swing and not (_tf3OnChart and chart_use_swing)
tf3_gp_use_custom = tf3_show_custom
tf3_gp_use_quick = tf3_show_quick and not (_tf3OnChart and chart_use_quick)

// Deduplicate TF slots — skip if a higher-priority slot already covers the same timeframe
_tf1_sec = tf1_tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(tf1_tf)
_tf2_sec = tf2_tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(tf2_tf)
_tf3_sec = tf3_tf == '' ? timeframe.in_seconds() : timeframe.in_seconds(tf3_tf)

tf1_active = tf1_on
tf2_active = tf2_on and not (tf1_on and _tf2_sec == _tf1_sec)
tf3_active = tf3_on and not (tf1_on and _tf3_sec == _tf1_sec) and not (tf2_active and _tf3_sec == _tf2_sec)

_chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds()
_sdActive = autoSDProfile('')
if tf1_active and _tf1_sec == _chartSec
    _sdActive := resolveSdProfile(tf1_sd_profile, tf1_tf)
else if tf2_active and _tf2_sec == _chartSec
    _sdActive := resolveSdProfile(tf2_sd_profile, tf2_tf)
else if tf3_active and _tf3_sec == _chartSec
    _sdActive := resolveSdProfile(tf3_sd_profile, tf3_tf)

_sdEnabled = sd_on and _sdActive != 'Off'

sd_atr_mult = _sdActive == 'Scalping' ? 1.0 : _sdActive == 'Swing' ? 1.0 : _sdActive == 'Intraday' ? 1.0 : sd_atr_mult_in
sd_lookback = _sdActive == 'Scalping' ? 5 : _sdActive == 'Swing' ? 10 : _sdActive == 'Intraday' ? 10 : sd_lookback_in
sd_retests = _sdActive == 'Scalping' ? 3 : _sdActive == 'Swing' ? 3 : _sdActive == 'Intraday' ? 3 : sd_retests_in
sd_max_zones = _sdActive == 'Scalping' ? 3 : _sdActive == 'Swing' ? 5 : _sdActive == 'Intraday' ? 5 : sd_max_zones_in
sd_overlap = (_sdActive == 'Scalping' ? 40.0 : _sdActive == 'Swing' ? 60.0 : _sdActive == 'Intraday' ? 50.0 : float(sd_overlap_thresh)) / 100.0
sd_max_height = _sdActive == 'Scalping' ? 1.5 : _sdActive == 'Swing' ? 2.0 : _sdActive == 'Intraday' ? 1.5 : sd_max_height_in

//#endregion

//#region Real OHLC Override
// Only call request.security when Use Real OHLC is on. The call is a per-bar
// cost even when the result is discarded, so gating it saves work on standard
// candle types where chart OHLC already equals real OHLC.
// ticker.standard strips the chart-type modifier (Heikin Ashi / Renko / Kagi)
// from the ticker id. Requesting plain syminfo.tickerid on a Heikin Ashi chart
// returns the SAME smoothed HA values — the whole point of this toggle was
// being silently defeated on the charts that need it most.
[r_open, r_high, r_low, r_close] = if use_real_ohlc
    request.security(ticker.standard(syminfo.tickerid), timeframe.period, [open, high, low, close])
else
    [open, high, low, close]
_o = r_open
_h = r_high
_l = r_low
_c = r_close
// Volume MA is only consumed when volume enhancement is on. Skip the ta.sma
// otherwise. Returning na here is safe — every consumer is gated by
// vol_enhance_on, so the na is never compared.
vol_sma = vol_enhance_on ? ta.sma(volume, vol_ma_len) : na
//#endregion

//#region MA Filter
calcMA(_type, _length, _src) =>
    _type == 'EMA' ? ta.ema(_src, _length) : ta.sma(_src, _length)

// Per-TF MA + trend helper — evaluated either directly (chart TF) or inside request.security (HTF slots)
calcMAFilter(_src) =>
    _fast = calcMA(ma_fast_type, ma_fast_length, _src)
    _slow = calcMA(ma_slow_type, ma_slow_length, _src)
    _tdBullRaw = ma_line_mode == 'Fast Line' ? _fast > _fast[1] : _fast > _slow
    _tdBearRaw = ma_line_mode == 'Fast Line' ? _fast < _fast[1] : _fast < _slow
    _tdB = trend_dir_bias == 'With Trend' ? _tdBullRaw : _tdBearRaw
    _tdBr = trend_dir_bias == 'With Trend' ? _tdBearRaw : _tdBullRaw
    [_fast, _slow, _tdB, _tdBr]

// Chart-TF MA + trend — used by chart GP profiles and by the on-chart plots at the bottom.
// Skip the EMA/SMA pair entirely when the filter is off and neither plot is shown — saves
// two ta.ema/sma calls per bar in the common case.
_chartMaNeeded = ma_filter != 'Off' or show_ma_fast or show_ma_slow
[chart_maFast, chart_maSlow, chart_tdBull, chart_tdBear] = if _chartMaNeeded
    calcMAFilter(use_real_ohlc ? _c : ma_source)
else
    [float(na), float(na), true, true]
ma_fast = chart_maFast
ma_slow = chart_maSlow
//#endregion

//#region Pivot Computation
computePivots(len, _hi, _lo, _vol, _volMA) =>
    ph = ta.pivothigh(_hi, len, len)
    pl = ta.pivotlow(_lo, len, len)
    var float _lastH = na
    var float _lastL = na
    var float _hVolFlag = 0.0
    var float _lVolFlag = 0.0
    if not na(ph)
        _lastH := ph
        _hVolFlag := _vol[len] > _volMA[len] ? 1.0 : 0.0
    if not na(pl)
        _lastL := pl
        _lVolFlag := _vol[len] > _volMA[len] ? 1.0 : 0.0
    [_lastH, _lastL, _hVolFlag, _lVolFlag]

// One combined data request per overlay slot: all four pivot profiles plus
// the Quick range in a single flattened tuple. Requesting once per slot
// instead of five times cuts the script's data-request count sharply and
// speeds loading. (Pine can't nest tuples inside a request expression, so
// this returns one flat 18-value tuple.)
slotData(int _scalpLen, int _intrLen, int _swingLen, int _customLen, int _qLen) =>
    [_sH, _sL, _sHV, _sLV] = computePivots(_scalpLen, _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
    [_iH, _iL, _iHV, _iLV] = computePivots(_intrLen, _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
    [_wH, _wL, _wHV, _wLV] = computePivots(_swingLen, _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
    [_cuH, _cuL, _cuHV, _cuLV] = computePivots(_customLen, _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
    [_qH, _qL] = quickRange(_qLen, _h, _l)
    [_sH, _sL, _sHV, _sLV, _iH, _iL, _iHV, _iLV, _wH, _wL, _wHV, _wLV, _cuH, _cuL, _cuHV, _cuLV, _qH, _qL]
//#endregion

//#region Timeframe Data
// One combined request per overlay slot (see slotData) — all four pivot
// profiles plus the Quick range arrive together; profiles the user hasn't
// ticked are simply ignored downstream (drawGP gates on its _on flag).
[tf1_H_scalp, tf1_L_scalp, tf1_hVol_scalp, tf1_lVol_scalp, tf1_H_intr, tf1_L_intr, tf1_hVol_intr, tf1_lVol_intr, tf1_H_swing, tf1_L_swing, tf1_hVol_swing, tf1_lVol_swing, tf1_H_custom, tf1_L_custom, tf1_hVol_custom, tf1_lVol_custom, tf1_H_quick, tf1_L_quick] = if tf1_active and (tf1_gp_use_scalping or tf1_gp_use_intraday or tf1_gp_use_swing or tf1_gp_use_custom or tf1_gp_use_quick)
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf1_tf, slotData(profilePivot(tf1_tf, 'Scalping'), profilePivot(tf1_tf, 'Intraday'), profilePivot(tf1_tf, 'Swing'), tf1_piv_distance, quickLen(tf1_tf)))
else
    [float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na)]

[tf2_H_scalp, tf2_L_scalp, tf2_hVol_scalp, tf2_lVol_scalp, tf2_H_intr, tf2_L_intr, tf2_hVol_intr, tf2_lVol_intr, tf2_H_swing, tf2_L_swing, tf2_hVol_swing, tf2_lVol_swing, tf2_H_custom, tf2_L_custom, tf2_hVol_custom, tf2_lVol_custom, tf2_H_quick, tf2_L_quick] = if tf2_active and (tf2_gp_use_scalping or tf2_gp_use_intraday or tf2_gp_use_swing or tf2_gp_use_custom or tf2_gp_use_quick)
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf2_tf, slotData(profilePivot(tf2_tf, 'Scalping'), profilePivot(tf2_tf, 'Intraday'), profilePivot(tf2_tf, 'Swing'), tf2_piv_distance, quickLen(tf2_tf)))
else
    [float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na)]

[tf3_H_scalp, tf3_L_scalp, tf3_hVol_scalp, tf3_lVol_scalp, tf3_H_intr, tf3_L_intr, tf3_hVol_intr, tf3_lVol_intr, tf3_H_swing, tf3_L_swing, tf3_hVol_swing, tf3_lVol_swing, tf3_H_custom, tf3_L_custom, tf3_hVol_custom, tf3_lVol_custom, tf3_H_quick, tf3_L_quick] = if tf3_active and (tf3_gp_use_scalping or tf3_gp_use_intraday or tf3_gp_use_swing or tf3_gp_use_custom or tf3_gp_use_quick)
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf3_tf, slotData(profilePivot(tf3_tf, 'Scalping'), profilePivot(tf3_tf, 'Intraday'), profilePivot(tf3_tf, 'Swing'), tf3_piv_distance, quickLen(tf3_tf)))
else
    [float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0, float(na), float(na)]

// Per-TF MA + trend flags — evaluated at each slot's timeframe.
// Skipped when the slot is disabled OR when the MA filter is off (drawGP
// short-circuits to true in that case, so the values are unused). This
// avoids three request.security calls every bar when the filter is off.
_maFilterOn = ma_filter != 'Off'
[tf1_maFast, tf1_maSlow, tf1_tdBull, tf1_tdBear] = if tf1_active and _maFilterOn
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf1_tf, calcMAFilter(use_real_ohlc ? _c : ma_source))
else
    [float(na), float(na), true, true]
[tf2_maFast, tf2_maSlow, tf2_tdBull, tf2_tdBear] = if tf2_active and _maFilterOn
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf2_tf, calcMAFilter(use_real_ohlc ? _c : ma_source))
else
    [float(na), float(na), true, true]
[tf3_maFast, tf3_maSlow, tf3_tdBull, tf3_tdBear] = if tf3_active and _maFilterOn
    request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf3_tf, calcMAFilter(use_real_ohlc ? _c : ma_source))
else
    [float(na), float(na), true, true]

// Chart-TF pivots — direct calls, no security needed (we're already on the chart timeframe).
// Each profile's pivothigh/pivotlow pair is only computed when that profile is enabled
// for the chart, saving up to 4 ta.pivot* calls per bar when only one profile is active.
[chart_H_scalp, chart_L_scalp, chart_hVol_scalp, chart_lVol_scalp] = if chart_use_scalp
    computePivots(profilePivot('', 'Scalping'), _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
else
    [float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0]
[chart_H_intr, chart_L_intr, chart_hVol_intr, chart_lVol_intr] = if chart_use_intr
    computePivots(profilePivot('', 'Intraday'), _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
else
    [float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0]
[chart_H_swing, chart_L_swing, chart_hVol_swing, chart_lVol_swing] = if chart_use_swing
    computePivots(profilePivot('', 'Swing'), _h, _l, volume, vol_sma)
else
    [float(na), float(na), 0.0, 0.0]
[chart_H_quick, chart_L_quick] = if chart_use_quick
    quickRange(quickLen(''), _h, _l)
else
    [float(na), float(na)]

//#endregion

//#region Helper — Volume-boosted color
boostColor(_baseColor, _isHighVol) =>
    _isHighVol ? color.new(_baseColor, math.max(color.t(_baseColor) - vol_transp_boost, 0)) : _baseColor
//#endregion

//#region Draw GP Boxes
// Hit-rate tallies per pivot profile (0 Scalping · 1 Intraday · 2 Swing ·
// 3 Custom), shared across chart and overlay slots. A GP counts as tested
// once price trades back into it; it then either holds (survives until a
// new pivot replaces it) or fails (invalidation closes it). Read by the
// Zone Dashboard's Hit-Rate rows.
var array<int> _hrHeld = array.new_int(4, 0)
var array<int> _hrFail = array.new_int(4, 0)

drawGP(_on, _H, _L, _boxColor, _txtColor, _maFast, _maSlow, _tdBull, _tdBear, _hVolFlag, _lVolFlag, _statIdx) =>
    var box _bullBox = na
    var box _bearBox = na
    var line _bullMidLine = na
    var line _bearMidLine = na
    var line _fibLine = na
    var label _bullAnchor = na
    var label _bearAnchor = na
    var int _hBar = na
    var int _lBar = na
    var int _bullInvalidCount = 0
    var int _bearInvalidCount = 0
    var color _bullBorderColor = na
    var color _bearBorderColor = na
    var bool _bullWarning = false
    var bool _bearWarning = false
    var bool _bullOutOfPlay = false
    var bool _bearOutOfPlay = false
    var bool _bullExtReached = false
    var bool _bearExtReached = false
    // Hit-rate tracking: has price entered the current active zone yet?
    var bool _bullTouched = false
    var bool _bearTouched = false
    var box _bullExtBox = na
    var box _bearExtBox = na
    var line _bullExtLine = na
    var line _bearExtLine = na
    var line _bullOteLine = na
    var line _bearOteLine = na
    var array<box> _closedBoxes = array.new_box()
    var array<int> _closedTypes = array.new_int()

    // A "new pivot" requires an actual change from one valid value to another.
    // Treating na → value as a new pivot (the previous behavior) caused the script's
    // first evaluated bar — limited by calc_bars_count — to synthesize a fake pivot
    // event using whatever stale _lastH/_lastL the inline or security-context
    // computePivots happened to hold from disjoint swings, producing a box whose
    // height = |old_lastH − old_lastL| could span the full chart. The slide block
    // then dragged that giant box forward every bar. Requiring a non-na predecessor
    // means we wait for a real pivot transition before drawing.
    // _on gate: with the combined per-slot data request, unticked profiles now
    // receive real pivot values instead of na — without the gate they would
    // still register "changes" and steal the Auto-mode ladder.
    _newHigh = _on and not na(_H) and _H != _H[1]
    _newLow = _on and not na(_L) and _L != _L[1]
    _changed = _newHigh or _newLow
    _gpChanged = _changed

    if _newHigh
        _hBar := bar_index
    if _newLow
        _lBar := bar_index

    if _on and not na(_H) and not na(_L) and _H > _L
        // Pivot-pair derived values (range, fib edges, MA filter, vol flags,
        // cosmetic offsets) only matter on bars where a pivot just formed.
        // Gating by _changed skips ~95% of bars where the GP isn't redrawn.
        if _changed
            _range = _H - _L

            // Bullish GP: 0.618–0.707 retracement from the high (pullback support)
            _bullHigh = _H - _range * _fibL1
            _bullLow = _H - _range * _fibL2

            // Bearish GP: 0.618–0.707 retracement from the low (rally resistance)
            _bearLow = _L + _range * _fibL1
            _bearHigh = _L + _range * _fibL2

            // MA filters
            _ppBull = ma_line_mode == 'Fast Line' ? _H > _maFast and _L > _maFast : _H > _maFast and _L > _maFast and _maFast > _maSlow
            _ppBear = ma_line_mode == 'Fast Line' ? _H < _maFast and _L < _maFast : _H < _maFast and _L < _maFast and _maFast < _maSlow
            _bullFilter = ma_filter == 'Off' ? true : ma_filter == 'Trend Direction' ? _tdBull : _ppBull
            _bearFilter = ma_filter == 'Off' ? true : ma_filter == 'Trend Direction' ? _tdBear : _ppBear

            // Volume flags — pivot high vol confirms bull GP, pivot low vol confirms bear GP
            _bullHV = vol_enhance_on and _hVolFlag > 0.5
            _bearHV = vol_enhance_on and _lVolFlag > 0.5

            // Cosmetic box edges — purely visual. Calculations (pivots, invalidation, volume)
            // are independent of these.
            _leftBar = bar_index - gp_left_offset
            _rightBar = bar_index + gp_right_offset

            // Fib line from older pivot to newer pivot — always reflects latest pivot pair
            line.delete(_fibLine)
            _fibLine := na
            if show_line and not na(_hBar) and not na(_lBar)
                if _lBar <= _hBar
                    _fibLine := line.new(_lBar, _L, _hBar, _H, style = _fibStyle, color = line_colour)
                else
                    _fibLine := line.new(_hBar, _H, _lBar, _L, style = _fibStyle, color = line_colour)

            // Bullish GP — only archived/redrawn when a new pivot HIGH forms.
            // A new low does NOT touch the bull box — the zone stays anchored to its originating pivot pair.
            if _newHigh
                // Hit-rate: the outgoing bull GP was tested and survived until
                // a fresh pivot replaced it — that counts as held.
                if not na(_bullBox) and _bullTouched
                    array.set(_hrHeld, _statIdx, array.get(_hrHeld, _statIdx) + 1)
                _bullTouched := false
                // Bullish GP — archive or delete
                if show_closed and not na(_bullBox)
                    box.set_bgcolor(_bullBox, closed_color)
                    box.set_border_color(_bullBox, closed_color)
                    box.set_text_color(_bullBox, closed_color)
                    array.push(_closedBoxes, _bullBox)
                    array.push(_closedTypes, 1)
                else
                    box.delete(_bullBox)
                line.delete(_bullMidLine)
                label.delete(_bullAnchor)
                _bullBox := na
                _bullMidLine := na
                _bullAnchor := na
                line.delete(_bullOteLine)
                _bullOteLine := na
                if _bullFilter
                    _bullColor = boostColor(_boxColor, _bullHV)
                    _bullLabel = show_bull_label ? (use_emoji ? '🐂 GP' : (use_short_labels ? 'BL' : 'Bull GP')) + (_bullHV and show_volume_stars ? ' ★' : '') : ''
                    _bullBox := box.new(_leftBar, _bullHigh, _rightBar, _bullLow, bgcolor = _bullColor, border_color = _bullColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = _bullLabel, text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.small)
                    _bullBorderColor := _bullColor
                    _bullWarning := false
                    _bullInvalidCount := 0
                    if show_mid
                        _mid = (_bullLow + _bullHigh) / 2
                        _midLeft = extend_mid_to_pivot and not na(_lBar) ? _lBar : _leftBar
                        _midRight = extend_mid_to_pivot ? bar_index + 1 : _rightBar
                        _bullMidLine := line.new(_midLeft, _mid, _midRight, _mid, style = _midStyle, color = mid_color, extend = mid_extend_right ? extend.right : extend.none)
                    if show_gp_anchor and not na(_lBar)
                        _bullAnchor := label.new(_lBar, _L, '', yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_circle, color = color.yellow, size = size.tiny)
                    if show_ote_line
                        _oteY = _H - _range * ote_line_level
                        _bullOteLine := line.new(_leftBar, _oteY, _rightBar, _oteY, style = line.style_dotted, color = color.new(_boxColor, 0))

                // Bull extension band + bonus line — anchored to the pivot HIGH, projected upward.
                // Extensions draw whenever the pivot pair is valid, independent of _bullFilter,
                // so users can see potential upside targets even when no active GP is drawn.
                box.delete(_bullExtBox)
                line.delete(_bullExtLine)
                _bullExtBox := na
                _bullExtLine := na
                _bullExtReached := false
                if show_gp_ext
                    _extLow = _H + _range * _fibL1
                    _extHigh = _H + _range * _fibL2
                    _bullExtBox := box.new(_leftBar, _extHigh, _rightBar, _extLow, bgcolor = _boxColor, border_color = _boxColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = show_ext_label ? 'Ex.' : '', text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_bottom)
                if show_gp_ext_line
                    _extY = _H + _range * (gp_ext_line_level - 1)
                    _bullExtLine := line.new(_leftBar, _extY, _rightBar, _extY, style = _midStyle, color = color.new(_boxColor, 0))

            // Bearish GP — only archived/redrawn when a new pivot LOW forms.
            // A new high does NOT touch the bear box — the zone stays anchored to its originating pivot pair.
            if _newLow
                // Hit-rate: the outgoing bear GP was tested and survived until
                // a fresh pivot replaced it — that counts as held.
                if not na(_bearBox) and _bearTouched
                    array.set(_hrHeld, _statIdx, array.get(_hrHeld, _statIdx) + 1)
                _bearTouched := false
                // Bearish GP — archive or delete
                if show_closed and not na(_bearBox)
                    box.set_bgcolor(_bearBox, closed_color)
                    box.set_border_color(_bearBox, closed_color)
                    box.set_text_color(_bearBox, closed_color)
                    array.push(_closedBoxes, _bearBox)
                    array.push(_closedTypes, -1)
                else
                    box.delete(_bearBox)
                line.delete(_bearMidLine)
                label.delete(_bearAnchor)
                _bearBox := na
                _bearMidLine := na
                _bearAnchor := na
                line.delete(_bearOteLine)
                _bearOteLine := na
                if _bearFilter
                    _bearColor = boostColor(_boxColor, _bearHV)
                    _bearLabel = show_bear_label ? (use_emoji ? '🐻 GP' : (use_short_labels ? 'BR' : 'Bear GP')) + (_bearHV and show_volume_stars ? ' ★' : '') : ''
                    _bearBox := box.new(_leftBar, _bearHigh, _rightBar, _bearLow, bgcolor = _bearColor, border_color = _bearColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = _bearLabel, text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.small)
                    _bearBorderColor := _bearColor
                    _bearWarning := false
                    _bearInvalidCount := 0
                    if show_mid
                        _mid = (_bearLow + _bearHigh) / 2
                        _midLeft = extend_mid_to_pivot and not na(_hBar) ? _hBar : _leftBar
                        _midRight = extend_mid_to_pivot ? bar_index + 1 : _rightBar
                        _bearMidLine := line.new(_midLeft, _mid, _midRight, _mid, style = _midStyle, color = mid_color, extend = mid_extend_right ? extend.right : extend.none)
                    if show_gp_anchor and not na(_hBar)
                        _bearAnchor := label.new(_hBar, _H, '', yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_circle, color = color.yellow, size = size.tiny)
                    if show_ote_line
                        _oteY = _L + _range * ote_line_level
                        _bearOteLine := line.new(_leftBar, _oteY, _rightBar, _oteY, style = line.style_dotted, color = color.new(_boxColor, 0))

                // Bear extension band + bonus line — anchored to the pivot LOW, projected downward.
                box.delete(_bearExtBox)
                line.delete(_bearExtLine)
                _bearExtBox := na
                _bearExtLine := na
                _bearExtReached := false
                if show_gp_ext
                    _extHigh = _L - _range * _fibL1
                    _extLow = _L - _range * _fibL2
                    _bearExtBox := box.new(_leftBar, _extHigh, _rightBar, _extLow, bgcolor = _boxColor, border_color = _boxColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = show_ext_label ? 'Ex.' : '', text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_bottom)
                if show_gp_ext_line
                    _extY = _L - _range * (gp_ext_line_level - 1)
                    _bearExtLine := line.new(_leftBar, _extY, _rightBar, _extY, style = _midStyle, color = color.new(_boxColor, 0))

        // Slide cosmetic edges each bar so the active box tracks current price.
        _leftExt = bar_index - gp_left_offset
        _rightExt = bar_index + gp_right_offset
        if not na(_bullBox)
            box.set_left(_bullBox, _leftExt)
            box.set_right(_bullBox, _rightExt)
            if not na(_bullMidLine)
                if extend_mid_to_pivot
                    line.set_x2(_bullMidLine, bar_index + 1)
                else
                    line.set_x1(_bullMidLine, _leftExt)
                    line.set_x2(_bullMidLine, _rightExt)
        else
            _bullInvalidCount := 0
        if not na(_bearBox)
            box.set_left(_bearBox, _leftExt)
            box.set_right(_bearBox, _rightExt)
            if not na(_bearMidLine)
                if extend_mid_to_pivot
                    line.set_x2(_bearMidLine, bar_index + 1)
                else
                    line.set_x1(_bearMidLine, _leftExt)
                    line.set_x2(_bearMidLine, _rightExt)
        else
            _bearInvalidCount := 0

        // Slide extension band/line edges so they track the current bar like the GPs do.
        if not na(_bullExtBox)
            box.set_left(_bullExtBox, _leftExt)
            box.set_right(_bullExtBox, _rightExt)
        if not na(_bearExtBox)
            box.set_left(_bearExtBox, _leftExt)
            box.set_right(_bearExtBox, _rightExt)
        if not na(_bullExtLine)
            line.set_x1(_bullExtLine, _leftExt)
            line.set_x2(_bullExtLine, _rightExt)
        if not na(_bearExtLine)
            line.set_x1(_bearExtLine, _leftExt)
            line.set_x2(_bearExtLine, _rightExt)
        if not na(_bullOteLine)
            line.set_x1(_bullOteLine, _leftExt)
            line.set_x2(_bullOteLine, _rightExt)
        if not na(_bearOteLine)
            line.set_x1(_bearOteLine, _leftExt)
            line.set_x2(_bearOteLine, _rightExt)

        // Hit-rate: mark the active GP as tested the first time price trades
        // into it (low reaches down into a bull zone, high reaches up into a
        // bear zone).
        if not na(_bullBox) and not _bullTouched and _l <= box.get_top(_bullBox)
            _bullTouched := true
        if not na(_bearBox) and not _bearTouched and _h >= box.get_bottom(_bearBox)
            _bearTouched := true

        // Optional active GP invalidation by consecutive bars beyond the zone
        if gp_invalidation_on
            _invRef = gp_invalidation_source == 'Open' ? _o : _c
            if not na(_bullBox)
                _bullBroken = _invRef < box.get_bottom(_bullBox)
                _bullInvalidCount := _bullBroken ? _bullInvalidCount + 1 : 0
                if _bullInvalidCount >= gp_invalidation_bars
                    if show_closed
                        box.set_bgcolor(_bullBox, closed_color)
                        box.set_border_color(_bullBox, closed_color)
                        box.set_text_color(_bullBox, closed_color)
                        array.push(_closedBoxes, _bullBox)
                        array.push(_closedTypes, 1)
                    else
                        box.delete(_bullBox)
                    line.delete(_bullMidLine)
                    label.delete(_bullAnchor)
                    line.delete(_bullOteLine)
                    _bullBox := na
                    _bullMidLine := na
                    _bullAnchor := na
                    _bullOteLine := na
                    _bullInvalidCount := 0
                    _gpChanged := true
                    array.set(_hrFail, _statIdx, array.get(_hrFail, _statIdx) + 1)
                    _bullTouched := false
                    if ext_link_invalidation
                        box.delete(_bullExtBox)
                        line.delete(_bullExtLine)
                        _bullExtBox := na
                        _bullExtLine := na
                else if gp_warn_on and _bullInvalidCount > 0
                    box.set_border_color(_bullBox, gp_warn_color)
                    _bullWarning := true
                else if gp_warn_on and _bullInvalidCount == 0 and _bullWarning
                    box.set_border_color(_bullBox, _bullBorderColor)
                    _bullWarning := false
            if not na(_bearBox)
                _bearBroken = _invRef > box.get_top(_bearBox)
                _bearInvalidCount := _bearBroken ? _bearInvalidCount + 1 : 0
                if _bearInvalidCount >= gp_invalidation_bars
                    if show_closed
                        box.set_bgcolor(_bearBox, closed_color)
                        box.set_border_color(_bearBox, closed_color)
                        box.set_text_color(_bearBox, closed_color)
                        array.push(_closedBoxes, _bearBox)
                        array.push(_closedTypes, -1)
                    else
                        box.delete(_bearBox)
                    line.delete(_bearMidLine)
                    label.delete(_bearAnchor)
                    line.delete(_bearOteLine)
                    _bearBox := na
                    _bearMidLine := na
                    _bearAnchor := na
                    _bearOteLine := na
                    _bearInvalidCount := 0
                    _gpChanged := true
                    array.set(_hrFail, _statIdx, array.get(_hrFail, _statIdx) + 1)
                    _bearTouched := false
                    if ext_link_invalidation
                        box.delete(_bearExtBox)
                        line.delete(_bearExtLine)
                        _bearExtBox := na
                        _bearExtLine := na
                else if gp_warn_on and _bearInvalidCount > 0
                    box.set_border_color(_bearBox, gp_warn_color)
                    _bearWarning := true
                else if gp_warn_on and _bearInvalidCount == 0 and _bearWarning
                    box.set_border_color(_bearBox, _bearBorderColor)
                    _bearWarning := false

        // Out-of-play highlight — runs after warn block so warn color always takes priority
        if gp_oop_on
            if not na(_bullBox) and not _bullWarning
                _bullOOP = _c < box.get_bottom(_bullBox)
                _bullOutOfPlay := _bullOOP
                box.set_border_color(_bullBox, _bullOOP ? gp_oop_color : _bullBorderColor)
            if not na(_bearBox) and not _bearWarning
                _bearOOP = _c > box.get_top(_bearBox)
                _bearOutOfPlay := _bearOOP
                box.set_border_color(_bearBox, _bearOOP ? gp_oop_color : _bearBorderColor)
        else
            if not na(_bullBox) and _bullOutOfPlay
                box.set_border_color(_bullBox, _bullBorderColor)
                _bullOutOfPlay := false
            if not na(_bearBox) and _bearOutOfPlay
                box.set_border_color(_bearBox, _bearBorderColor)
                _bearOutOfPlay := false

        // Extension reached-marking — recolor the target band once price first tags it.
        // Bull ext sits above the pivot high (price reaches up into its lower edge);
        // bear ext sits below the pivot low (price reaches down into its upper edge).
        if ext_mark_reached
            if not na(_bullExtBox) and not _bullExtReached and _h >= box.get_bottom(_bullExtBox)
                _bullExtReached := true
                box.set_bgcolor(_bullExtBox, ext_reached_color)
                box.set_border_color(_bullExtBox, ext_reached_color)
            if not na(_bearExtBox) and not _bearExtReached and _l <= box.get_top(_bearExtBox)
                _bearExtReached := true
                box.set_bgcolor(_bearExtBox, ext_reached_color)
                box.set_border_color(_bearExtBox, ext_reached_color)

    // Closed GP cleanup
    if show_closed
        if closed_deletion == 'Max Count' or closed_deletion == 'Both'
            while array.size(_closedBoxes) > max_closed
                box.delete(array.remove(_closedBoxes, 0))
                array.remove(_closedTypes, 0)
        if closed_deletion == 'Price Invalidation' or closed_deletion == 'Both'
            if array.size(_closedBoxes) > 0
                for i = array.size(_closedBoxes) - 1 to 0 by 1
                    _cBox = array.get(_closedBoxes, i)
                    _cType = array.get(_closedTypes, i)
                    if (_cType == 1 and _c < box.get_bottom(_cBox)) or (_cType == -1 and _c > box.get_top(_cBox))
                        box.delete(array.remove(_closedBoxes, i))
                        array.remove(_closedTypes, i)

    [_bullBox, _bearBox, _bullExtBox, _bearExtBox, _gpChanged, _newHigh, _newLow]

// Quick GP — the "eyeball" profile. Draws a Golden Pocket straight from the highest high
// and lowest low of a lookback window, with no pivot confirmation. Both the bull GP
// (retracement down from the range high — pullback support) and the bear GP (retracement
// up from the range low — pullback resistance) are drawn at once and updated in place every
// bar as the window's range evolves, like glancing at the chart and drawing a pocket on the
// visible swing. No archiving, no invalidation, no MA filter — it always reflects the live
// range. Returns the same tuple shape as drawGP so confluence, alerts, and the ladder treat
// it exactly like a pivot-based GP.
drawQuickGP(bool _on, float _H, float _L, color _boxColor, color _txtColor) =>
    var box _bullBox = na
    var box _bearBox = na
    var line _bullMid = na
    var line _bearMid = na
    var box _bullExtBox = na
    var box _bearExtBox = na
    var line _bullExtLine = na
    var line _bearExtLine = na
    var line _bullOte = na
    var line _bearOte = na

    // Hold the range steady through the forming candle: only re-read the rolling high/low
    // on a confirmed bar, so the pocket updates once per new candle instead of jiggling
    // tick-by-tick on the live bar. Historical bars are always confirmed, so they update
    // every bar as expected.
    var float _drawH = na
    var float _drawL = na
    if barstate.isconfirmed
        _drawH := _H
        _drawL := _L

    _newHigh = _on and not na(_drawH) and (na(_drawH[1]) or _drawH != _drawH[1])
    _newLow = _on and not na(_drawL) and (na(_drawL[1]) or _drawL != _drawL[1])
    _gpChanged = _newHigh or _newLow

    if _on and not na(_drawH) and not na(_drawL) and _drawH > _drawL
        _range = _drawH - _drawL
        _bullHigh = _drawH - _range * _fibL1
        _bullLow = _drawH - _range * _fibL2
        _bearLow = _drawL + _range * _fibL1
        _bearHigh = _drawL + _range * _fibL2
        _leftBar = bar_index - gp_left_offset
        _rightBar = bar_index + gp_right_offset
        _midExtend = mid_extend_right ? extend.right : extend.none

        // Bull GP box (in place)
        _bullLabel = show_bull_label ? (use_emoji ? '🐂 GP' : (use_short_labels ? 'BL' : 'Bull GP')) : ''
        if na(_bullBox)
            _bullBox := box.new(_leftBar, _bullHigh, _rightBar, _bullLow, bgcolor = _boxColor, border_color = _boxColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = _bullLabel, text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.small)
        else
            box.set_lefttop(_bullBox, _leftBar, _bullHigh)
            box.set_rightbottom(_bullBox, _rightBar, _bullLow)
            box.set_bgcolor(_bullBox, _boxColor)
            box.set_border_color(_bullBox, _boxColor)
            box.set_text(_bullBox, _bullLabel)

        // Bear GP box (in place)
        _bearLabel = show_bear_label ? (use_emoji ? '🐻 GP' : (use_short_labels ? 'BR' : 'Bear GP')) : ''
        if na(_bearBox)
            _bearBox := box.new(_leftBar, _bearHigh, _rightBar, _bearLow, bgcolor = _boxColor, border_color = _boxColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = _bearLabel, text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.small)
        else
            box.set_lefttop(_bearBox, _leftBar, _bearHigh)
            box.set_rightbottom(_bearBox, _rightBar, _bearLow)
            box.set_bgcolor(_bearBox, _boxColor)
            box.set_border_color(_bearBox, _boxColor)
            box.set_text(_bearBox, _bearLabel)

        // Midpoint lines
        if show_mid
            _bullMidY = (_bullHigh + _bullLow) / 2
            if na(_bullMid)
                _bullMid := line.new(_leftBar, _bullMidY, _rightBar, _bullMidY, style = _midStyle, color = mid_color, extend = _midExtend)
            else
                line.set_xy1(_bullMid, _leftBar, _bullMidY)
                line.set_xy2(_bullMid, _rightBar, _bullMidY)
                line.set_extend(_bullMid, _midExtend)
            _bearMidY = (_bearHigh + _bearLow) / 2
            if na(_bearMid)
                _bearMid := line.new(_leftBar, _bearMidY, _rightBar, _bearMidY, style = _midStyle, color = mid_color, extend = _midExtend)
            else
                line.set_xy1(_bearMid, _leftBar, _bearMidY)
                line.set_xy2(_bearMid, _rightBar, _bearMidY)
                line.set_extend(_bearMid, _midExtend)
        else
            line.delete(_bullMid)
            line.delete(_bearMid)
            _bullMid := na
            _bearMid := na

        // OTE sweet-spot lines (single retracement level inside each pocket)
        if show_ote_line
            _bullOteY = _drawH - _range * ote_line_level
            _bearOteY = _drawL + _range * ote_line_level
            if na(_bullOte)
                _bullOte := line.new(_leftBar, _bullOteY, _rightBar, _bullOteY, style = line.style_dotted, color = color.new(_boxColor, 0))
            else
                line.set_xy1(_bullOte, _leftBar, _bullOteY)
                line.set_xy2(_bullOte, _rightBar, _bullOteY)
                line.set_color(_bullOte, color.new(_boxColor, 0))
            if na(_bearOte)
                _bearOte := line.new(_leftBar, _bearOteY, _rightBar, _bearOteY, style = line.style_dotted, color = color.new(_boxColor, 0))
            else
                line.set_xy1(_bearOte, _leftBar, _bearOteY)
                line.set_xy2(_bearOte, _rightBar, _bearOteY)
                line.set_color(_bearOte, color.new(_boxColor, 0))
        else
            line.delete(_bullOte)
            line.delete(_bearOte)
            _bullOte := na
            _bearOte := na

        // Extension bands (same fib spacing mirrored outward from each edge)
        if show_gp_ext
            _bullExtLow = _drawH + _range * _fibL1
            _bullExtHigh = _drawH + _range * _fibL2
            _bearExtHigh = _drawL - _range * _fibL1
            _bearExtLow = _drawL - _range * _fibL2
            if na(_bullExtBox)
                _bullExtBox := box.new(_leftBar, _bullExtHigh, _rightBar, _bullExtLow, bgcolor = _boxColor, border_color = _boxColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = show_ext_label ? 'Ex.' : '', text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_bottom)
            else
                box.set_lefttop(_bullExtBox, _leftBar, _bullExtHigh)
                box.set_rightbottom(_bullExtBox, _rightBar, _bullExtLow)
                box.set_bgcolor(_bullExtBox, _boxColor)
                box.set_border_color(_bullExtBox, _boxColor)
                box.set_text(_bullExtBox, show_ext_label ? 'Ex.' : '')
            if na(_bearExtBox)
                _bearExtBox := box.new(_leftBar, _bearExtHigh, _rightBar, _bearExtLow, bgcolor = _boxColor, border_color = _boxColor, border_style = _borderStyle, text = show_ext_label ? 'Ex.' : '', text_color = _txtColor, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_bottom)
            else
                box.set_lefttop(_bearExtBox, _leftBar, _bearExtHigh)
                box.set_rightbottom(_bearExtBox, _rightBar, _bearExtLow)
                box.set_bgcolor(_bearExtBox, _boxColor)
                box.set_border_color(_bearExtBox, _boxColor)
                box.set_text(_bearExtBox, show_ext_label ? 'Ex.' : '')
        else
            box.delete(_bullExtBox)
            box.delete(_bearExtBox)
            _bullExtBox := na
            _bearExtBox := na

        // Bonus extension line at the user-defined level
        if show_gp_ext_line
            _extLnCol = color.new(_boxColor, 0)
            _bullExtY = _drawH + _range * (gp_ext_line_level - 1)
            _bearExtY = _drawL - _range * (gp_ext_line_level - 1)
            if na(_bullExtLine)
                _bullExtLine := line.new(_leftBar, _bullExtY, _rightBar, _bullExtY, style = _midStyle, color = _extLnCol)
            else
                line.set_xy1(_bullExtLine, _leftBar, _bullExtY)
                line.set_xy2(_bullExtLine, _rightBar, _bullExtY)
                line.set_color(_bullExtLine, _extLnCol)
            if na(_bearExtLine)
                _bearExtLine := line.new(_leftBar, _bearExtY, _rightBar, _bearExtY, style = _midStyle, color = _extLnCol)
            else
                line.set_xy1(_bearExtLine, _leftBar, _bearExtY)
                line.set_xy2(_bearExtLine, _rightBar, _bearExtY)
                line.set_color(_bearExtLine, _extLnCol)
        else
            line.delete(_bullExtLine)
            line.delete(_bearExtLine)
            _bullExtLine := na
            _bearExtLine := na
    else
        box.delete(_bullBox)
        box.delete(_bearBox)
        line.delete(_bullMid)
        line.delete(_bearMid)
        box.delete(_bullExtBox)
        box.delete(_bearExtBox)
        line.delete(_bullExtLine)
        line.delete(_bearExtLine)
        line.delete(_bullOte)
        line.delete(_bearOte)
        _bullBox := na
        _bearBox := na
        _bullMid := na
        _bearMid := na
        _bullExtBox := na
        _bearExtBox := na
        _bullExtLine := na
        _bearExtLine := na
        _bullOte := na
        _bearOte := na

    [_bullBox, _bearBox, _bullExtBox, _bearExtBox, _gpChanged, _newHigh, _newLow]

// Tiny corner tag showing the source timeframe on an overlay-TF GP box (e.g. '15m').
// Follows the active box's top-left corner each bar and clears when the box is gone, or
// when _tf is empty — same-timeframe slots pass '' so no redundant tag is drawn. Call once
// per overlay-TF profile with its bull/bear boxes; chart-TF profiles don't call it.
drawTfTag(box _bullBox, box _bearBox, string _tf, color _col) =>
    var label _bullTag = na
    var label _bearTag = na
    if not na(_bullBox) and _tf != ''
        if na(_bullTag)
            _bullTag := label.new(box.get_left(_bullBox), box.get_top(_bullBox), _tf, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_lower_right, color = color.new(_col, 100), textcolor = color.new(_col, 0), size = size.tiny)
        else
            label.set_xy(_bullTag, box.get_left(_bullBox), box.get_top(_bullBox))
            label.set_text(_bullTag, _tf)
            label.set_textcolor(_bullTag, color.new(_col, 0))
    else
        label.delete(_bullTag)
        _bullTag := na
    if not na(_bearBox) and _tf != ''
        if na(_bearTag)
            _bearTag := label.new(box.get_left(_bearBox), box.get_top(_bearBox), _tf, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_label_lower_right, color = color.new(_col, 100), textcolor = color.new(_col, 0), size = size.tiny)
        else
            label.set_xy(_bearTag, box.get_left(_bearBox), box.get_top(_bearBox))
            label.set_text(_bearTag, _tf)
            label.set_textcolor(_bearTag, color.new(_col, 0))
    else
        label.delete(_bearTag)
        _bearTag := na
    _bearTag

// Overlay-TF corner tags — empty when the slot's timeframe equals the chart's, so only
// genuinely different-timeframe GPs get tagged.
_tf1Tag = _tf1_sec != _chartSec ? prettyTF(tf1_tf) : ''
_tf2Tag = _tf2_sec != _chartSec ? prettyTF(tf2_tf) : ''
_tf3Tag = _tf3_sec != _chartSec ? prettyTF(tf3_tf) : ''

// Chart-TF GPs (drawn from chart data using Chart GP Profile 1 & 2)
[chart_bull_scalp, chart_bear_scalp, chart_bullExt_scalp, chart_bearExt_scalp, chart_chg_scalp, chart_hChg_scalp, chart_lChg_scalp] = drawGP(chart_use_scalp, chart_H_scalp, chart_L_scalp, chart_color_scalp, _labelTextColor, chart_maFast, chart_maSlow, chart_tdBull, chart_tdBear, chart_hVol_scalp, chart_lVol_scalp, 0)
manageLadder('Chart-Scalp', chart_pin_scalp, chart_chg_scalp, chart_hChg_scalp, chart_lChg_scalp, false, not na(chart_bull_scalp), not na(chart_bear_scalp), chart_H_scalp, chart_L_scalp, chart_color_scalp)
[chart_bull_intr, chart_bear_intr, chart_bullExt_intr, chart_bearExt_intr, chart_chg_intr, chart_hChg_intr, chart_lChg_intr] = drawGP(chart_use_intr, chart_H_intr, chart_L_intr, chart_color_intr, _labelTextColor, chart_maFast, chart_maSlow, chart_tdBull, chart_tdBear, chart_hVol_intr, chart_lVol_intr, 1)
manageLadder('Chart-Intr', chart_pin_intr, chart_chg_intr, chart_hChg_intr, chart_lChg_intr, false, not na(chart_bull_intr), not na(chart_bear_intr), chart_H_intr, chart_L_intr, chart_color_intr)
[chart_bull_swing, chart_bear_swing, chart_bullExt_swing, chart_bearExt_swing, chart_chg_swing, chart_hChg_swing, chart_lChg_swing] = drawGP(chart_use_swing, chart_H_swing, chart_L_swing, chart_color_swing, _labelTextColor, chart_maFast, chart_maSlow, chart_tdBull, chart_tdBear, chart_hVol_swing, chart_lVol_swing, 2)
manageLadder('Chart-Swing', chart_pin_swing, chart_chg_swing, chart_hChg_swing, chart_lChg_swing, false, not na(chart_bull_swing), not na(chart_bear_swing), chart_H_swing, chart_L_swing, chart_color_swing)
[chart_bull_quick, chart_bear_quick, chart_bullExt_quick, chart_bearExt_quick, chart_chg_quick, chart_hChg_quick, chart_lChg_quick] = drawQuickGP(chart_use_quick, chart_H_quick, chart_L_quick, chart_color_quick, _labelTextColor)
